{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set","id":904325,"title":"[Ex3] Not the God-King of Gaps? Holes in the Solar Charm Set","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-31T11:45:35-07:00","id":904325,"title":"[Ex3] Not the God-King of Gaps? Holes in the Solar Charm Set","content":"So... I've seen a bunch of comments in threads that there are &quot;holes&quot; in the Ex3 Solar Charm Set. No gaps really stood out in my very quick skim read of the charm set, yet I haven't had a chance to give the Ex3 Core a through read. Thus my questions:<br /> <br /> What are the &quot;gaps&quot; in the Ex3 Solar charm set?<br /> <br /> Could these gaps reveal anything about the charm sets of the other splats?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T11:54:57-07:00","id":904331,"title":"","content":"Not really any big gap beside the obvious stuffs, like Solars obviously aren't shapeshifting into beasts (Lunars) or transforming into monsters (Infernals) or the overkills/fatalities (Abyssals).<br /> <br /> Plus with the backer charms , we are looking at 80 more solar charms coming up relatively soon. Granted Holden and John did say the backer charms are more like the kind of &quot;I'm the best and let me show you my powers!&quot; charms...so expect to see all kind of over the top effects, which I'm looking forward to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T11:59:26-07:00","id":904336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904331#post904331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or the overkills/fatalities (Abyssals).</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly aren't stunting hard enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:11:45-07:00","id":904343,"title":"","content":"I feel like War has a bit of a gap, it focuses almost entirely on modifying the Strategic Warfare system (which should be its focus), but is kinda missing any charms that deal with the aspects of being a general outside of battle and that system.<br /> <br /> I would have liked to see War have more colourful and diverse charms like say Sail. A big chunck of sail plays on the Naval Combat system, but it also has a good handful of charms more to do with things tangental to fighting at sea and sailing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:26:19-07:00","id":904356,"title":"","content":"Brawl has almost no defense.<br /> Craft has one big hole of being annoying to play ;-)<br /> Thrown is only for silent assassins, no good things for other character types.<br /> Lore has not enough &quot;Lore&quot; things, it seems like half of it is Wyld-Shaping and one quarter is motes/health/willpower sending/stealing.<br /> Occult has almost none of Sorcery-based Charms.<br /> Survival is one big pet tree and pretty much nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:40:08-07:00","id":904361,"title":"","content":"I agree with Survival benefiting from more than the huge pet focus, and War could use some smaller coordination benefits.<br /> I think Thrown could use a lot more options, though it's not QUITE as narrow some some folks have played it out to be.<br /> I agree that Brawn has few defense options which is technically a hole, but to me that feels like design choice and I'm personally ok with it (pure opinion).<br /> I don't know if I could stand any more Lore charms, but it is a bit light on the knowledge front (though what it has is potent).<br /> I'd like to see art creation charms for like painting or such things. It feels like they should be in Craft or Performance, but the Linguistics charm-set is so well constructed for what I'd like to see them do.<br /> I actually disagree with the idea that Occult should even have any Sorcery enhancers (too easy to explode into &quot;too good&quot; in my humble opinion) but I would like to see a bit more in there beyond the &quot;trap, see, and manipulate spirits&quot; area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:42:00-07:00","id":904363,"title":"","content":"<b>Thrown </b>has: An accuracy booster [permitting range benefits as if one step closer], an opening decisive attack against a slow opponent to injure or kill them, a JB enhancer, a penalty inflicter, a cover-negator, a range-extender, a full excellency boost that negates dodge and damages everything around the target, another JB enhancer which grants [Dexterity] attacks, a silencing attack, a stealthy attack, a couple distract or disarm boosters, a stealthy attack boost, an AOE attack, a situational base initiative booster, a reflexive attack after the stealthy attack, another distract booster, a decisive attack booster, a distract booster that adds a disarm, a reflexive attack after disarming, an ambush booster, a decisive attack that is boosted by anima and harms demons, ghosts, and other 'creatures of the night', and a multiple attacker charm.<br /> <br /> Roughly 4/24 [silencing, stealthy, reflexive post-stealthy, and ambush booster], yeah, it's 100% only good for stealthy sneaky assassins and has no value whatsoever to someone focusing on Disarm and Distract gambits [trick shots] or just generally being the first to attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Survival </b>is heavily pet-based, but there's still more non-pet charms in it than there were in 2e.<br /> <br /> <b>Lore</b> is very heavy on the Wyld-Shaping, could use other stuff.<br /> <br /> I also get the feeling that <b>Brawl</b>'s deliberate lack of easy, routine defenses was a stylistic decision; you could create homebrew defensive charms for it but by raw it seems like it's heavily leaning towards all-out offense compared to Melee's balanced approach","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 05-31-2016, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:46:09-07:00","id":904368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904356#post904356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brawl has almost no defense.<br /> Craft has one big hole of being annoying to play ;-)<br /> Thrown is only for silent assassins, no good things for other character types.<br /> Lore has not enough &quot;Lore&quot; things, it seems like half of it is Wyld-Shaping and one quarter is motes/health/willpower sending/stealing.<br /> Occult has almost none of Sorcery-based Charms.<br /> Survival is one big pet tree and pretty much nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last may be my biggest gap complaint. I wanted to see a variety of Charms along the lines of Transcendent Desert Creature and instead got a ruleset for being a Pok\u00e9mon Trainer.<br /> <br /> Even though it hampers my first character's combat effectiveness, I don't really mind the lack of defense in Brawl so much because it seems that thematically Dodge and Resistance cover that shortfall, and if one's concept needs a more skillful unarmed block/parry sort of defense there's a good selection of Martial Arts styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:46:21-07:00","id":904369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904356#post904356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brawl has almost no defense.<br /> Craft has one big hole of being annoying to play ;-)<br /> Thrown is only for silent assassins, no good things for other character types.<br /> Lore has not enough &quot;Lore&quot; things, it seems like half of it is Wyld-Shaping and one quarter is motes/health/willpower sending/stealing.<br /> Occult has almost none of Sorcery-based Charms.<br /> Survival is one big pet tree and pretty much nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brawl has some decent defense charms but IMO why not just take dodge for even better ones.<br /> <br /> Can't dissagree on Craft...<br /> <br /> Thrown pretty much models what I would exspect it to, tactical trick shots and precise applications of violence. What other aspects would you like it to have that wouldnt be cannibalizing Archery?<br /> <br /> Lore is pretty padded out with Wyld Shaping but it has always been the most awkward Ability to write so no big surprise there.<br /> <br /> WHY ARENT THERE ANY SORCEROUS WORKING CHARMS!!! The Crafting system has the entire Craft tree dedicated to it but Sorcerous Workings have nothing in Occult. The closest I have come is when I used Burning Exorcism Technique and Soul Projection Method to use a nephwrack's exorcized curse as materials in a sorcerous working to scry it's location.<br /> <br /> The Familiar tree is awesome but wraps back on itself so much that its really bulky even for a supernal Survival character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:55:38-07:00","id":904370,"title":"","content":"I assumed the Lore &quot;Knowing things charms&quot; fall under the &quot;Create fact&quot; lore charms. I'm going to assume crazy stupid research tricks are going to the Sidereal Charm Set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:06:51-07:00","id":904375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904370#post904370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed the Lore &amp;quot;Knowing things charms&amp;quot; fall under the &amp;quot;Create fact&amp;quot; lore charms. I'm going to assume crazy stupid research tricks are going to the Sidereal Charm Set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similarly I have a feeling that the lack of small group tactics charms in War is because the DB will have them...I guess Solars can't work together!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:14:51-07:00","id":904381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904375#post904375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Similarly I have a feeling that the lack of small group tactics charms in War is because the DB will have them...I guess Solars can't work together!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Solars fill the Prima Donna Exalt Niche. &quot;I don't need help! I can do the work of five people!&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder if the &quot;Dump me naked in the wilderness and I will thrive&quot; charms will go to Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-31-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:24:27-07:00","id":904387,"title":"","content":"There is one gap I sometimes feel is there in EX3, the gap where the system can't handle supernal power essence users who are playing in it LOL. I really can't wait to try playing basically anything but Solaroids, I think the system will shine even more in the context of slightly less overwhelming charms and dice pools. To be honest I actually want to try Solars without supernals and a 1wp surcharge on any excellency over 5 dice just to see how it plays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:44:01-07:00","id":904408,"title":"","content":"I doubt coordinated attacks based on rolling War is a thing in this system anymore, which, y'know, thank God.<br /> <br /> (Now I am posting from a phone)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:44:20-07:00","id":904409,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Archery:</b> Little support for non-bow Archery weapons.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Athletics:</b> Not much in the flexibility/contortionist area of Athletics.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Awareness: </b>is 90% random ways to add dice, rather than actual capability expansion (the fluffy descriptions don't really help for implementation.)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brawl: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Light on Defense (expected), light on crippling/maiming actions (unexpected).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bureaucracy: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is all about markets/dealing and &quot;leading.&quot; Can't say it really has a gap, because it doesn't have much of a system to plug into.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craft: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Charm set is fanatically devoted to clicking cookies, with very little utlity or &quot;can-do&quot; added on.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dodge: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Narrow, but uh...it's Dodge? Working as intended IMHO.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Still a bit of a grab-bag, but surprisingly light on simple Resolve/Guile boosting, overall.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Investigation: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You're Sherlock Holmes. No, really, that's your character's concept, stop having ideas.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Linguistics: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Has very little to do with languages.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lore: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As others have said, pretty light on charms actually related to the subject at hand. Creation's greatest scholars are apparently mote batteries.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medicine: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;I'm House without the 40 minutes of being wrong every episode,&quot; and that's it. No neat powers, no new avenues of setting interaction.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Occult: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Apparently the only use for Occult is beating/imprisoning/eating spirits. Who knew.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Performance: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Assumes a highly limited definition of the word Performance, and pays for it.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resistance: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Few</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> non-combat applications of Resistance.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Survival: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">alias Survival=&quot;Pokemaster&quot;</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Socialize: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Little support for manipulating or changing cultural norms (which is something Solars do).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thrown: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There have already been multiple threads on the problem.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">War: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Train troops and be a superb strategist, but next to zero support outside of it. War got short-changed pretty hard.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:08:26-07:00","id":904432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904408#post904408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt coordinated attacks based on rolling War is a thing in this system anymore, which, y'know, thank God.<br /> <br /> (Now I am posting from a phone)</div> </div> </div> </div>They were such a pain, but I think there is still room for some War charms that benefit characters working with a shared set of tactics, like a SWAT team clearing a building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:11:23-07:00","id":904434,"title":"","content":"War, huh? What is it good for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:29:49-07:00","id":904449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904432#post904432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were such a pain, but I think there is still room for some War charms that benefit characters working with a shared set of tactics, like a SWAT team clearing a building.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> SWAT teams working together seem very Dragonblooded. Solars are more Die Hard, one man army type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:38:26-07:00","id":904456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904356#post904356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Survival is one big pet tree and pretty much nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> So much this.<br /> <br /> What happened to charms like in 2.5e where you made a sanctuary of safe land even in the middle of the Labyrinth where you could find food and rest? What about charm ideas to bless a land with abundant fertility?<br /> <br /> Sorcery yea, but sorcery shouldn't be the only ones doing it. Outside of pets Survival feels super dietary.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:49:18-07:00","id":904472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904456#post904456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This.<br /> <br /> So much this.<br /> <br /> What happened to charms like in 2.5e where you made a sanctuary of safe land even in the middle of the Labyrinth where you could find food and rest? What about charm ideas to bless a land with abundant fertility?<br /> <br /> Sorcery yea, but sorcery shouldn't be the only ones doing it. Outside of pets Survival feels super dietary.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It also has precisely one charm associated with tracking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:12:15-07:00","id":904489,"title":"","content":"I think it's a bit silly to assert that any one group has more of a lock on the &quot;fight as a group thing&quot; than any other, considering that this is a game for 2-6 players. Is &quot;one man army&quot; really much better than &quot;guards a territory and drives everybody away from it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think tactics between players is a bit weird to abstract. I also think that, considering how small battle groups can get, you're better off using one of those as your Howling Commandos, rather than the other players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:21:45-07:00","id":904496,"title":"","content":"Even though the section on designing Solar charms declares it to be possible, there is no charm for shattering bones with a shout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:28:54-07:00","id":904502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904409#post904409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Athletics:</b> Not much in the flexibility/contortionist area of Athletics.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think due to its applications (fitting through small holes and such), contortionists and flexibility actually belongs into larceny... But then, larceny only has that &quot;walk through a closed door&quot; charm, and no &quot;fit through any hole your head fits through, and possibly even smaller holes&quot;-charm. And it already is a huge mix of various skills, so branching this one out might be better...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 05-31-2016, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:29:40-07:00","id":904503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904489#post904489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a bit silly to assert that any one group has more of a lock on the &quot;fight as a group thing&quot; than any other, considering that this is a game for 2-6 players. Is &quot;one man army&quot; really much better than &quot;guards a territory and drives everybody away from it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think tactics between players is a bit weird to abstract. I also think that, considering how small battle groups can get, you're better off using one of those as your Howling Commandos, rather than the other players.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think Solars fight in a group more like the Avengers. They each have their own strengths and usually fight their enemies one on one, even if they are all in the same fight. Occasionally they will combo powers (like Hawkeye shooting Ant-Man) but that is rare. Dragonblooded always work together. Hell, maybe they will be able to combo different charms with other Dragonblooded. Who knows?<br /> <br /> Anywho, I tend to consider &quot;Dragonblooded build groups&quot; while, if I remember correctly, you disagreed with that assertion, so this may be one of those &quot;Agree to disagree&quot; topics. <br /> <br /> In my head this is how a Solar and a Dragonblooded would work together.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded: What the fuck happened to the plan?<br /> Solar: I made the plan better.<br /> Dragonblooded: Didn't we have a talk about changing the plan halfway though the plan!?<br /> Solar: Stop bitching. It worked, didn't it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-31-2016, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:56:04-07:00","id":904513,"title":"","content":"To paraphrase Jim Butcher's Cursor's Fury:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You've been trained to duel, or fight in a loose, fast group of individual warriors. The front line of a Legion battlefield is a different world.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;How so?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Legionaries aren't warriors, Tavi. They are professional soldiers.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What's the difference?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Warriors<i> fight.</i> Legionaries fight <i>together</i>. It isn't about being the best swordsman. It's about forming a whole that is stronger than the sum of the individuals in it.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Solar : Warrior; Dragonblooded : Legionnaire","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:59:17-07:00","id":904516,"title":"","content":"Holden has repeatedly said that playing combat as everybody dividing one on one is a fool's game, and I see several areas in the system around that.<br /> <br /> So you notice how many Brawl Charms are designed around enemies having Onslaught penalties? That would definitely be helped by having your friends all attack a key target ahead of you. Heck, they don't even need to be any good at it; they just need to make their pitiful attacks to level the penalties, then let the Brawler wade in to take advantage.<br /> <br /> Being able to do more than just stand around in a fight of your combat Abilities are low: another repeated assertion of the developers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904513#post904513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To paraphrase Jim Butcher's Cursor's FurSolar : Warrior; Dragonblooded : Legionnaire</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that play when there are only one to give of you?<br /> <br /> <b>Battle groups</b> are legionnaires, not Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-31-2016, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:00:31-07:00","id":904518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904496#post904496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though the section on designing Solar charms declares it to be possible, there is no charm for shattering bones with a shout.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon-Wracking Shout?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:01:21-07:00","id":904520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904516#post904516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holden has repeatedly said that playing combat as everybody dividing one on one is a fool's game, and I see several areas in the system around that.<br /> <br /> So you notice how many Brawl Charms are designed around enemies having Onslaught penalties? That would definitely be helped by having your friends all attack a key target ahead of you. Heck, they don't even need to be any good at it; they just need to make their pitiful attacks to level the penalties, then let the Brawler wade in to take advantage.<br /> <br /> Being able to do more than just stand around in a fight of your combat Abilities are low: another repeated assertion of the developers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So then small group tactics isn't a gap in the Solar charm set. They are in Brawl instead of War. <br /> <br /> Hey, I can be wrong. I'll admit I am wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:05:07-07:00","id":904523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904409#post904409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Awareness: </b>is 90% random ways to add dice, rather than actual capability expansion (the fluffy descriptions don't really help for implementation.)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely wrong. All the Keen (Sense) and Unsurpassed (Sense) abilities are packed with capability extension, and those &quot;random&quot; ways to add dice are extremely useful when contesting enemy stealth attempts - what I would consider to be one of the most important awareness capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:12:03-07:00","id":904530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904409#post904409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Archery:</b> Little support for non-bow Archery weapons.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Athletics:</b> Not much in the flexibility/contortionist area of Athletics.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Awareness: </b>is 90% random ways to add dice, rather than actual capability expansion (the fluffy descriptions don't really help for implementation.)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brawl: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Light on Defense (expected), light on crippling/maiming actions (unexpected).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bureaucracy: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is all about markets/dealing and &quot;leading.&quot; Can't say it really has a gap, because it doesn't have much of a system to plug into.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craft: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Charm set is fanatically devoted to clicking cookies, with very little utlity or &quot;can-do&quot; added on.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dodge: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Narrow, but uh...it's Dodge? Working as intended IMHO.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Still a bit of a grab-bag, but surprisingly light on simple Resolve/Guile boosting, overall.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Investigation: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You're Sherlock Holmes. No, really, that's your character's concept, stop having ideas.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Linguistics: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Has very little to do with languages.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lore: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As others have said, pretty light on charms actually related to the subject at hand. Creation's greatest scholars are apparently mote batteries.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medicine: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;I'm House without the 40 minutes of being wrong every episode,&quot; and that's it. No neat powers, no new avenues of setting interaction.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Occult: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Apparently the only use for Occult is beating/imprisoning/eating spirits. Who knew.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Performance: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Assumes a highly limited definition of the word Performance, and pays for it.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resistance: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Few</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> non-combat applications of Resistance.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Survival: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">alias Survival=&quot;Pokemaster&quot;</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Socialize: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Little support for manipulating or changing cultural norms (which is something Solars do).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thrown: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There have already been multiple threads on the problem.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">War: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Train troops and be a superb strategist, but next to zero support outside of it. War got short-changed pretty hard.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Most of these are non-issues. In the example of Archery, Brawl, and Performance it's design choices and narrative space (say, Performance has to draw some differentiation from Presence, if they both continue to exist as separate Things. Whether they actually <i>need </i>to is another story - the 25 Abilities frankly seem bloated and out of date today, but that's not gonna change anytime soon, so here we are). For Athletics, Resistance, and Linguistics, the things you mention are solidly covered by the notion of &quot;why does this even need a roll/specific widget effect?&quot; This falls a bit into Survival too, as in, &quot;how many survivalist tropes really need their own Charm to flesh out beyond just an Excellency?&quot; Capability expansion is built into Awareness through the dice, and would be more appropriate for Solars than, say, random other senses.<br /> <br /> Thrown I have agreed on this notion 100%.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904432#post904432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were such a pain, but I think there is still room for some War charms that benefit characters working with a shared set of tactics, like a SWAT team clearing a building.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems more of a DB thing than a solar thing. And again we run into &quot;what is the appropriate scope of this effect across multiple splats trying to channel different aspects of the concept of 'Ability excellence'?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:27:11-07:00","id":904543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904363#post904363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roughly 4/24 [silencing, stealthy, reflexive post-stealthy, and ambush booster], yeah, it's 100% only good for stealthy sneaky assassins and has no value whatsoever to someone focusing on Disarm and Distract gambits [trick shots] or just generally being the first to attack.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903013-what-s-wrong-with-thrown\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ng-with-thrown</a> Please come here ;-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904369#post904369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thrown pretty much models what I would exspect it to, tactical trick shots and precise applications of violence. What other aspects would you like it to have that wouldnt be cannibalizing Archery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different type of Thrown characters, ones that fight more openly. With unique Thrown weapons and their users like Sango and her Hiraikotsu, Glaive from Krull, Xena and her chakrams (I think, didn't watch that one), Fuuma Shurikens, almost all Touhou cast (shining fields and patters of magical bullets), Captain America and his shield, Sokka and his boomerang... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904363#post904363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also get the feeling that <b>Brawl</b>'s deliberate lack of easy, routine defenses was a stylistic decision; you could create homebrew defensive charms for it but by raw it seems like it's heavily leaning towards all-out offense compared to Melee's balanced approach</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very deliberate, but it's still a hole ;-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904369#post904369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brawl has some decent defense charms but IMO why not just take dodge for even better ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't have problems with it, just saying there's a hole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:36:16-07:00","id":904547,"title":"","content":"What kind of gaps are we talking about specifically? There are things Solar charms don't currently do, there are things Solar charms shouldn't do, there are things Charms in general shouldn't do, and there are things Abilities shouldn't do. <br /> <br /> Like, a circle using small group tactics? It's just a question of the players coordinating their character's actions and to use the right gambits and attacks at the right moment. I would be very surprised if it ever got covered by DB War Charms, barring a significant reinterpretation of what the War Ability means for DBs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:36:58-07:00","id":904549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904523#post904523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is absolutely wrong. All the Keen (Sense) and Unsurpassed (Sense) abilities are packed with capability extension</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. Awareness has 22 Charms, and 12 of them add new capabilities. That said, half of those are Keen/Unsurpassed Sense Charms. That said, the impressive descriptions in the Keen/Unsurpassed Senses Charms are really hard to adjudicate as an ST without any kind of guidance on difficulties of rolls or any other mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904523#post904523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and those &quot;random&quot; ways to add dice are extremely useful when contesting enemy stealth attempts - what I would consider to be one of the most important awareness capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those other 10 are really boring dice tricks and while yes, they help you notice hidden enemies, and yes, that's an important aspect of Awareness, personally it's not at all something I get excited about. If you're not interested in dice tricks to find hidden characters, and especially if you're not interested in one or two of the Keen (Sense) Charms, there's not a lot to get in Awareness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:39:53-07:00","id":904553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904549#post904549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you're not interested in dice tricks to find hidden characters, and especially if you're not interested in one or two of the Keen (Sense) Charms, there's not a lot to get in Awareness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's <i>almost</i> like saying, &quot;If you're not interested in punching people, there's not a lot to get in Brawl.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:40:17-07:00","id":904554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904530#post904530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This falls a bit into Survival too, as in, &quot;how many survivalist tropes really need their own Charm to flesh out beyond just an Excellency?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They could've gone the Sail route and had a bunch of Charms that are not directly related to survival, but being a Survivalist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:43:52-07:00","id":904557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904553#post904553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's <i>almost</i> like saying, &quot;If you're not interested in punching people, there's not a lot to get in Brawl.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a helluva a lot more to Awareness than finding hidden enemies. And funny enough, if you're not into punching people, there's a ton still to get in Brawl for grappling and defense. Like 20 Charms. Which is about as much as Awareness gets in total.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:45:28-07:00","id":904560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904553#post904553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's <i>almost</i> like saying, &quot;If you're not interested in punching people, there's not a lot to get in Brawl.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I miss a little some Bullet Time/Aim Enhancers/Otherworldly Perception effects ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:30:57-07:00","id":904614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904560#post904560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I miss a little some Bullet Time/Aim Enhancers/Otherworldly Perception effects ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullet time would be the join battle boosts. Aim enhancers are in Archery/Thrown. Otherworldy peerception are in Occult/Integrity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:43:58-07:00","id":904622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904554#post904554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could've gone the Sail route and had a bunch of Charms that are not directly related to survival, but being a Survivalist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more along the lines of what I was thinking. Sail gets a little too focused on the assumption that one is a ship's captain higher up the trees, but the basics are versatile and highly flavorful. I think Salty Dog Method may be my favorite Charm, full stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:44:41-07:00","id":904623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904614#post904614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullet time would be the join battle boosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't seem like that to me. And Bullet Time is not only active at the start of battle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904614#post904614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aim enhancers are in Archery/Thrown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and I can't use them with Brawl/Melee/MA. Something in Awareness would be very nice, even if other abilities have them - some design space overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904614#post904614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherworldy peerception are in Occult/Integrity</div> </div> </div> </div>And some should be here. Another overlap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:51:57-07:00","id":904626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904523#post904523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is absolutely wrong. All the Keen (Sense) and Unsurpassed (Sense) abilities are packed with capability extension..</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I thought that the first time I read them. On re-reading...not so much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904530#post904530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of these are non-issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for you to judge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904560#post904560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I miss a little some Bullet Time/Aim Enhancers/Otherworldly Perception effects ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want aim enhancers and otherworldly perception, check out BlueWinds' rewrite. There are some in there.<br /> <br /> Bullet time is hard to make a Charm for, though, since it's more of a camera trick than an actual ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:03:16-07:00","id":904634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904623#post904623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and I can't use them with Brawl/Melee/MA. Something in Awareness would be very nice, even if other abilities have them - some design space overlap.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is you can justify absolutely anything with awareness.<br /> <br /> Defense boost, Accuracy boosts, Damage boosts, Read Intentions boosts etc.<br /> <br /> To much overlap would just cheapen the choice of Supernatural","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:08:25-07:00","id":904639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904614#post904614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullet time would be the join battle boosts. Aim enhancers are in Archery/Thrown. Otherworldy peerception are in Occult/Integrity</div> </div> </div> </div>(Awareness has <i>one</i> dedicated JB booster, Awakened Eye. It has a bunch of other charms that boost it as an ancillary effect, and a bunch of them are limited, like to enemies you can't see.)<br /> <br /> Why yes, one of the downsides to Awareness is that there are a fair number of perception charms in other abilities! The JB and aim boosters in Archery and Thrown. The spirit/essence perception stuff in Occult and a few specialized effects in Integrity. There's also a couple effects in Sail like Tide-Carried Omens and a couple in Linguistics like Discerning Savant's Eye and Swift Sage's Eye. You could even say Investigation gets some of what Awareness could have. A lot of what could be Awareness is instead elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T00:18:32-07:00","id":904764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904554#post904554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could've gone the Sail route and had a bunch of Charms that are not directly related to survival, but being a Survivalist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sail is a very, very situational ability, in that, if you're on a boat it's hella important and if you're not, it's pretty useless. Sail charms get a bunch extra packed into them to make it a worthwhile purchase in games that don't have sail as their primary focus.<br /> <br /> Survival is useful in many more different situations, so it doesn't get the additional capability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T01:27:56-07:00","id":904786,"title":"","content":"I have a real problem with linguistics not being useful in spreading ideas and changing the opinions of large populations. Most of linguistics, in fact, seems to be aimed more at assassins and spies then it is at scholars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:10:39-07:00","id":904795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>7 questions vanquish god</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904786#post904786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a real problem with linguistics not being useful in spreading ideas and changing the opinions of large populations. Most of linguistics, in fact, seems to be aimed more at assassins and spies then it is at scholars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm? Are we wanting a charm that accomplishes this with an action or are we looking for charms we have that can acheive this effect? Because a Linguist's influence does not fade from the paper it is written on and influence can be targeted generally. Adding speed writing into the mix and a quick Project to spread your new Zine-of-Absolutely-No-Influence-What-So-Ever-No-Siree-Bob can proliferate and influence large swaths of people.<br /> <br /> The only thing stopping this is the rampant illiteracy facing Creation but there are linguistics charms for that too! Have your zine read aloud by any you read it, spreading its influence to share folded in with the general message of Peace (it's Peace we want, right?) above and beyond one lonely studio.<br /> <br /> (I hope that was helpful)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:30:27-07:00","id":904804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904409#post904409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Socialize: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Little support for manipulating or changing cultural norms (which is something Solars do).</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't these end up coming out as charms because they were just too good in 2nd ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:51:23-07:00","id":904814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904804#post904804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't these end up coming out as charms because they were just too good in 2nd ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but what I think he meant is that they threw the baby out with the bathwater. Meaning just because an execution is flawed, doesn't mean you have to throw out all the good points it had as well as the bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:54:00-07:00","id":904815,"title":"","content":"Some of it's in bureaucracy now. Which I think is a fine place for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T03:37:05-07:00","id":904828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904795#post904795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmm? Are we wanting a charm that accomplishes this with an action or are we looking for charms we have that can achieve this effect? Because a Linguist's influence does not fade from the paper it is written on and influence can be targeted generally. Adding speed writing into the mix and a quick Project to spread your new Zine-of-Absolutely-No-Influence-What-So-Ever-No-Siree-Bob can proliferate and influence large swaths of people.<br /> <br /> The only thing stopping this is the rampant illiteracy facing Creation but there are linguistics charms for that too! Have your zine read aloud by any you read it, spreading its influence to share folded in with the general message of Peace (it's Peace we want, right?) above and beyond one lonely studio.<br /> <br /> (I hope that was helpful)</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game i came up with the same answers that you did. A creative reading of Whirling Brush Method and Flawless Brush Discipline allows the solar to replicate a work composed with an excellency or Flowing Elegant Hand quickly and cheaply. However, at this point i encountered two problems:<br /> 1. There is no system meant to deal with the spreading social influences in such a manner. How would my success be measured? What effects would it generate?<br /> 2. The charm support within linguistics for actual writing is minimal at best. if memory serves, the charms i listed above are the only charms meant to directly supplement the writing process itself. That forced me to branch into presence - something i initially didn't want my character to do.<br /> <br /> i would also love some charms that were aimed directly at spreading ideas and changing society with linguistics. So i find its apparent focus on assassination and spy-work quite frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","user":"7 questions vanquish god","date":". 06-01-2016, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:02:53-07:00","id":904895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904814#post904814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but what I think he meant is that they threw the baby out with the bathwater. Meaning just because an execution is flawed, doesn't mean you have to throw out all the good points it had as well as the bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Some people felt the 2E Socialize charms made remolding societies and cultural norms too easy, and the same effects would be wildly out of proportion with the overall lower power level of Ex3. But, it doesn't follow that those type of effects should be absent, just that they should be scaled back in effect, or that they should be highly involved actions, like Wyld-Shaping (though probably not that crunchy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:59:53-07:00","id":904932,"title":"","content":"Why would Linguistics Charms cover languages? Languages are a Merit now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:07:36-07:00","id":904934,"title":"","content":"Because that's literally what Linguistics means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T08:56:17-07:00","id":904985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904934#post904934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's literally what Linguistics means?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuuuuuup. There's a lot that could be done with memes, creating/modifying connotations in languages, making new words that create Intimacies, and of course making your own language that encourages/discourages certain modes of thought (Big Brother is totally a Zenith).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:02:20-07:00","id":904987,"title":"","content":"Lingusitics also means the use and study of language, which the ability and charms are all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T10:37:21-07:00","id":905046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904639#post904639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Awareness has <i>one</i> dedicated JB booster, Awakened Eye. It has a bunch of other charms that boost it as an ancillary effect, and a bunch of them are limited, like to enemies you can't see.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Some offer only incidental non-cap-breaking boosts, but others like Eyeless Harbinger Awareness, Knowing Beyond Silence and Inner Eye Focus are essentially fairly powerful JB boosters that also contest stealth/larceny actions. It's not that they're limited so much as that you cannot combine IEF with the other two, as it requires seeing the target and the other two require not doing so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T11:55:21-07:00","id":905087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904520#post904520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So then small group tactics isn't a gap in the Solar charm set. They are in Brawl instead of War.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI wouldn't phrase it like that. It's not a case of small unit tactics being a function of the mechanics at all; they're part of how players are assumed and incentivized to coordinate their actions in the course of play. Small unit tactics are not a function of Brawl, they're just something that it can benefit from because of how it was made to function.<br /> <br /> See also anything in Melee or Dodge or Resistance that enhances one's capacity to Defend Other(s), or how Thrown aids in distract gambits.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:01:35-07:00","id":905091,"title":"","content":"Something I saw touched on briefly but not really discussed: raising social defenses.<br /> <br /> I was <i>flabbergasted</i> when I realized that there are no Integrity Charms for pushing your Resolve beyond what an Excellency can do. None. No cap-breaking bonus in the vein of Reed In The Wind, no math tricks a la Drifting Leaf Elusion, none of the &quot;subtract enemy successes&quot; tech which show up all over the Solar charmset. If another supernatural being tries to persuade you of something, they <i>will</i> succeed. Don't waste motes - plan to spend Willpower.<br /> <br /> P.S.: Yes, there are effects to increase your mote economy for Resolve, or which ignore penalties. No, that's not the same thing.<br /> P.P.S.: Also, I will allow it is possible that the intent of Charms such as Stubborn Boar Defense and Temptation-Resisting Stance is that they should count as non-Charm bonuses, but I am legitimately unsure, and when in doubt, I assume the intent is to use the rules as written. I will point out that Undying Solar Resolve looks suspiciously like a Charm written as &quot;subtract enemy successes,&quot; then changed later, so I suspect that the lack of social defenses is deliberate, for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:08:34-07:00","id":905094,"title":"","content":"Do any of the suggested supernatural beings besides Mara have an especially high social pool, with powers to boost it? I mean, assuming a Solar who is not having somebody try to persuade them through a Major or higher Intimacy, in which case I would rather find the difficulty in not being persuaded to be the point.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd say the best defence, for everybody, is to not let devious actors ever gain much insight into what you care about in the first place. Your second line of defence is having things that you care about as much as or more than in order to keep you focused on your own goals.<br /> <br /> I dislike the idea of being able to boost Resolve too much, because then you rather override the point of the interesting Intimacy based social interaction system in the first place.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Hmm, Fakharu does have a fairly decent one at that, as well as a powerful (if limited) social Charm, but he's a high spiritual functionary, you'd expect that. On the other hand, there can still be penalties, depending on what he's asking of you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-01-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:35:38-07:00","id":905103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904932#post904932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Linguistics Charms cover languages? Languages are a Merit now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they do. That's part of what Linguistics does. See: the Excellent Emissary's Tongue tree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905091#post905091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I saw touched on briefly but not really discussed: raising social defenses.<br /> <br /> I was <i>flabbergasted</i> when I realized that there are no Integrity Charms for pushing your Resolve beyond what an Excellency can do. None. No cap-breaking bonus in the vein of Reed In The Wind, no math tricks a la Drifting Leaf Elusion, none of the &quot;subtract enemy successes&quot; tech which show up all over the Solar charmset. If another supernatural being tries to persuade you of something, they <i>will</i> succeed. Don't waste motes - plan to spend Willpower.<br /> <br /> P.S.: Yes, there are effects to increase your mote economy for Resolve, or which ignore penalties. No, that's not the same thing.<br /> P.P.S.: Also, I will allow it is possible that the intent of Charms such as Stubborn Boar Defense and Temptation-Resisting Stance is that they should count as non-Charm bonuses, but I am legitimately unsure, and when in doubt, I assume the intent is to use the rules as written. I will point out that Undying Solar Resolve looks suspiciously like a Charm written as &quot;subtract enemy successes,&quot; then changed later, so I suspect that the lack of social defenses is deliberate, for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, never noticed that.<br /> <br /> Gotta be deliberate. Not sure why they'd do it, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905094#post905094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do any of the suggested supernatural beings besides Mara have an especially high social pool, with powers to boost it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't many. Then again, there aren't many with especially high combat pools either. And we still have plenty of cap shenanigans in Dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:53:27-07:00","id":905115,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I find it interesting that the same player base which can complain about Solars always being better than everybody else at everything will also enthusiastically complain about a Solar Charmset that leaves room for other Exalt types to be good at some things in their own ways. Is it perhaps possible that these so-called gaps are not oversights, but the result of a deliberate design decision to define the expression of Solar excellence with regards to the game's Abilities differently than that of other, not-yet-published Exalted?<br /> <br /> Do we really want Solars to stake out <i>all </i>the best design space before anybody else even comes on to the scene?<br /> <br /> Do we <i>really</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:57:43-07:00","id":905118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905115#post905115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I find it interesting that the same player base which can complain about Solars always being better than everybody else at everything will also enthusiastically complain about a Solar Charmset that leaves room for other Exalt types to be good at some things in their own ways. Is it perhaps possible that these so-called gaps are not oversights, but the result of a deliberate design decision to define the expression of Solar excellence with regards to the game's Abilities differently than that of other, not-yet-published Exalted?<br /> <br /> Do we really want Solars to stake out <i>all </i>the best design space before anybody else even comes on to the scene?<br /> <br /> Do we <i>really</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit I started this thread to mine the gaps in the Solar Charm set for ideas on what the other splat's charms would look like. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:04:25-07:00","id":905125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905115#post905115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I find it interesting that the same player base which can complain about Solars always being better than everybody else at everything will also enthusiastically complain about a Solar Charmset that leaves room for other Exalt types to be good at some things in their own ways. Is it perhaps possible that these so-called gaps are not oversights, but the result of a deliberate design decision to define the expression of Solar excellence with regards to the game's Abilities differently than that of other, not-yet-published Exalted?<br /> <br /> Do we really want Solars to stake out <i>all </i>the best design space before anybody else even comes on to the scene?<br /> <br /> Do we <i>really</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we just like to be contrary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:05:06-07:00","id":905127,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's what the writers had in mind, going by their comments. Which is good, because trying to balance Solars and Lunars by making all the Solar Thrown Charms ninja-y (or all the Craft Charms number-crunchy, or all the Survival Charms pet-y, etc) is an absolutely doomed endeavour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:16:45-07:00","id":905132,"title":"","content":"Looking back on Survival with an eye toward leaving its wider applications to Lunars, I guess the few non-familiar general Charms will do. I still think I'd have preferred them to be broken up by environment type or Direction, though, rather than one-Charm-fits-all-environments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:31:12-07:00","id":905182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905103#post905103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta be deliberate. Not sure why they'd do it, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI think they don't want to give Solars in general, and players in particular, an easy out from the social influence system.<br /> <br /> It's like, if you have a Guild antagonist who tries to convince somebody to not kill them and leave their organisation alone because otherwise something will kill half the people in Nexus, the question of whether or not that works hinges mostly on whether the character has a Principle or Tie concerned with the people of Nexus, rather than the character being completely unmoved because they can make their Resolve insurmountable anyway and it comes down to if the player is convinced or cares.<br /> <br /> (People talk so much about how they don't need systems to help portray things like character rationality, and yet so many discussions of this scenario have people assert that a Solar would perfectly know whether or not they can outdo the Guildsman's kill switch rather than being hesitant in the heat of the moment, if they're not just making calculated risks)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:43:17-07:00","id":905196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905091#post905091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I saw touched on briefly but not really discussed: raising social defenses.<br /> <br /> I was <i>flabbergasted</i> when I realized that there are no Integrity Charms for pushing your Resolve beyond what an Excellency can do. None. No cap-breaking bonus in the vein of Reed In The Wind, no math tricks a la Drifting Leaf Elusion, none of the &quot;subtract enemy successes&quot; tech which show up all over the Solar charmset. If another supernatural being tries to persuade you of something, they <i>will</i> succeed. Don't waste motes - plan to spend Willpower.<br /> <br /> P.S.: Yes, there are effects to increase your mote economy for Resolve, or which ignore penalties. No, that's not the same thing.<br /> P.P.S.: Also, I will allow it is possible that the intent of Charms such as Stubborn Boar Defense and Temptation-Resisting Stance is that they should count as non-Charm bonuses, but I am legitimately unsure, and when in doubt, I assume the intent is to use the rules as written. I will point out that Undying Solar Resolve looks suspiciously like a Charm written as &quot;subtract enemy successes,&quot; then changed later, so I suspect that the lack of social defenses is deliberate, for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Righteous Lion Defense forces a reroll, and Unhesitating Dedication is a potentially very nasty success remover. Beyond that, you've got Temptation-Resisting Stance aka Infinite Resolve Mastery. When you're packing a static Resolve of 11, rejecting anything that manages to overcome it for only a single point of willpower is a bargain.<br /> <br /> But wait, there's more! Since Willpower is indescribably precious, you can just use Spirit-Maintaining Maneuver to spend essence instead. Add in Undying Solar Resolve and you'll be at least mote neutral on average.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T15:03:36-07:00","id":905210,"title":"","content":"Why is Willpower so precious? I understood that perception before to be because you needed it to activate your combos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T15:11:41-07:00","id":905212,"title":"","content":"You know, I find myself in something of an odd position regarding this thread. I am an EX3 booster, I support the devs maintaining control of the line to see it held together by one vision, even if it's one I don't agree with. You might expect to find me writing a defense of some of the criticisms of the charm trees, but for the most part, the community has identified the same gaps I saw in the playtest, for the most part, and I happen to agree especially in the cases of Survival and Thrown especially.<br /> <br /> I don't have much to add on how to fix that, as I don't want to create re-vamps of entire charm trees and clearer intended playstyle choices within them, and if I was going to do that I might as well write my own game. I would happily play EX3 as is, but that doesn't mean these things don't bother me.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T16:06:27-07:00","id":905241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905210#post905210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is Willpower so precious? I understood that perception before to be because you needed it to activate your combos.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 3e it's much harder to regenerate. In 2e 2-die stunts were like popcorn, virtues allowed 2-3 WP a Night, and other sources. In 3e you get 1 per night and a level two stunt is something that defines a scene, so it's quite a bit harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T16:44:38-07:00","id":905257,"title":"","content":"But is it a disaster if you're caught out without it?<br /> <br /> \u200bIncidentally, I wonder if anybody else has considered how Limit Break being the easiest way to restore Willpower creates an incentive for players to continuously expose their characters to their Trigger and defy their Intimacies.<br /> <br /> How's that for a gradual, insidious corruption? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T17:09:18-07:00","id":905270,"title":"","content":"I know a number of the stronger high level charms use wp,and it makes social manipulation a lot easier. Haven't encountered it, so can't say if it's disastrous, but definitely dangerous..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T17:21:55-07:00","id":905276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905257#post905257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is it a disaster if you're caught out without it?</div> </div> </div> </div>For sorcerers certainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T17:33:37-07:00","id":905281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905276#post905276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sorcerers certainly.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSee, that's why you transform yourself into somebody whose spilt blood turns into attack scorpions.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:13:17-07:00","id":905299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905196#post905196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Righteous Lion Defense forces a reroll</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOnly to a single kind of social action against a single Principle.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would find that the level of dedication that having such an inviolable Principle makes it the kind of thing that can be readily taken note of, which can make it easier for the right kind of character to tailor their arguments to exploit it, while making it harder to weaken the Principle to not be so extreme; if people realise that nothing ever moves you from a position of conquering Great Forks, they might start deciding that relating things to conquering Great Forks is a good way to get you over to their way of thinking, and of course they'll be right.<br /> <br /> I think straightforward Resolve boosters would detract from the drama entailed by those interactions and observations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:27:18-07:00","id":905307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905276#post905276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sorcerers certainly.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only need a single point of wp though, to cast terrestrial spells again and again, as most only cost 1wp which is then refunded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T19:53:36-07:00","id":905343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905046#post905046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some offer only incidental non-cap-breaking boosts, but others like Eyeless Harbinger Awareness, Knowing Beyond Silence and Inner Eye Focus are essentially fairly powerful JB boosters that also contest stealth/larceny actions. It's not that they're limited so much as that you cannot combine IEF with the other two, as it requires seeing the target and the other two require not doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eyeless Harbinger only works if you can't see your opponent and is within short range, and that's relatively rare circumstances in my experience. Knowing Beyond Silence is quite good, but since again you can only use it if you can't see your opponent, it's not going to see a lot of use. Unless you're character is blind. (Or closing their eyes? Does that even count?) Then both of these are fantastic.<br /> <br /> I'll grant you Inner Eye Focus, (and Blink to be honest), but that means you only get access to more than one generally useful JB booster if you happen to have a character that fits having Keen Sight. And that sorta sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T20:56:26-07:00","id":905381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905196#post905196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Righteous Lion Defense forces a reroll, and Unhesitating Dedication is a potentially very nasty success remover. Beyond that, you've got Temptation-Resisting Stance aka Infinite Resolve Mastery. When you're packing a static Resolve of 11, rejecting anything that manages to overcome it for only a single point of willpower is a bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're totally right about Righteous Lion Defense and Unhesitating Dedication! I should have been more clear: I'm not concerned with having Intimacies eroded. I'm more concerned with Twisted Words Technique, Memory-Reweaving, or similar tricks which bypass (or hijack!) your Intimacies to get right to the mind control - there are no cap-breakers to defend against that. Temptation-Resisting Stance is an AWFUL deal - spend WP to set up defenses which your enemy will bypass, forcing you to spend more Willpower. Fun for the whole Circle!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905343#post905343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll grant you Inner Eye Focus, (and Blink to be honest), but that means you only get access to more than one generally useful JB booster if you happen to have a character that fits having Keen Sight. And that sorta sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real tragedy is the Taste &amp; Smell crowd.<br /> <br /> Sight is amazing - it gets huge dice-trick-boosted schenanigans for Join Battle, opposing Larceny, and beating Stealth. Hearing/Touch is okay - it gets an even stronger trick than Sight, but only against stealth (including Join Battle versus Stealthed enemies). And Taste/Smell gets... a rock. Which is to say, conditional efficiency boosts if they have an Intimacy for a Stealthed person... and nothing else. No cap-breaking (that the other subtrees don't get, too), no reasonably-common cases where they reign supreme, nothing. How big of a deal are those dice tricks? At Essence 5 and against equal opposition, it winds up some 7-11 average successes behind the other senses. Never specialize for Taste/Smell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T21:01:19-07:00","id":905384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905182#post905182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think they don't want to give Solars in general, and players in particular, an easy out from the social influence system.<br /> <br /> It's like, if you have a Guild antagonist who tries to convince somebody to not kill them and leave their organisation alone because otherwise something will kill half the people in Nexus, the question of whether or not that works hinges mostly on whether the character has a Principle or Tie concerned with the people of Nexus, rather than the character being completely unmoved because they can make their Resolve insurmountable anyway and it comes down to if the player is convinced or cares.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think cap-breakers are needed there. 11 Resolve is more than enough to shut down mortal social shenanigans, barring an exceptional opponent rolling very well with help from your Intimacies.<br /> <br /> So the thing you're worried about is already the case. That can't be why they chose to make the Resolve cap firmer than the Parry/Evasion caps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905212#post905212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I find myself in something of an odd position regarding this thread. I am an EX3 booster...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I don't think it's healthy to define yourself like that. Don't be a booster or a hater, just be a person with opinions that are mostly positive or negative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905257#post905257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is it a disaster if you're caught out without it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Disaster might be an overstatement, but having no willpower makes quite a few important Charms unavailable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T21:02:05-07:00","id":905385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905257#post905257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is it a disaster if you're caught out without it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your playstyle.<br /> <br /> Some characters, such as Brawlers, can mount an extremely effective offensive with very little if any WP.<br /> <br /> Others, like Shining Point Stylists, need it absolutely or they cannot launch their best attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T21:18:11-07:00","id":905394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905307#post905307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You only need a single point of wp though, to cast terrestrial spells again and again, as most only cost 1wp which is then refunded.</div> </div> </div> </div>One failed spell and you are just as screwed as without Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T21:51:05-07:00","id":905401,"title":"","content":"If you don't have Willpower, a supernaturally-potent social character can make you do virtually anything.<br /> <br /> Your GM might not actually have this come up! Also, they might rule that when you fill in your Incapacitated level with damage, you get knocked out, fall off a waterfall, and eventually wash up on shore somewhere, alive and free. That's a valid GMing style, and one I tend towards myself... but nobody uses it as the basis to argue that running out of Health Levels isn't actually bad.<br /> <br /> Having no Willpower is bad. Like, &quot;your life is over&quot; kinda bad, if the right kind of enemy is nearby and the GM isn't merciful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T23:08:01-07:00","id":905420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905381#post905381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Temptation-Resisting Stance is an AWFUL deal - spend WP to set up defenses which your enemy will bypass, forcing you to spend more Willpower. Fun for the whole Circle!</div> </div> </div> </div>If your whole Circle has that up, it's not being reliably beaten by anything less than a full Solar-level dice pool. 20 dice will average 4m via Undying Solar Resolve, enough to power Spirit-Maintaining Maneuver even if, improbably, every attempt is successful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're totally right about Righteous Lion Defense and Unhesitating Dedication! I should have been more clear: I'm not concerned with having Intimacies eroded. I'm more concerned with Twisted Words Technique, Memory-Reweaving, or similar tricks which bypass (or hijack!) your Intimacies to get right to the mind control - there are no cap-breakers to defend against that. </div> </div> </div>Those just bounce right off of Invincible Solar Aegis. If you didn't have that available for whatever reason then Transcendent Hero's Meditation can shatter them after the fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:39:12-07:00","id":905501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905384#post905384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think cap-breakers are needed there. 11 Resolve is more than enough to shut down mortal social shenanigans, barring an exceptional opponent rolling very well with help from your Intimacies.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bLet me see...<br /> <br /> I think there may be a few things that can get Resolve up to eleven, so can you tell me which one you have in mind so that I can check back on its weaknesses, limitations, or unsustainable costs?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the thing you're worried about is already the case.</div> </div> </div> </div> As I'm reading the Charms, that really does not seem to be the case to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disaster might be an overstatement, but having no willpower makes quite a few important Charms unavailable.</div> </div> </div> </div> But not to the extent of Second Edition, where it was needed to sustain paranoia combos, yes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't have Willpower, a supernaturally potent social character can make you do virtually anything</div> </div> </div> </div> Good God, what kind of Intimacies does your character have?!<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this whole conversation has made me look back over the Integrity Charms, and I'm finding myself perplexed at every statement that Integrity is a soft option for Supernal Ability; so many of those powers present absolutely fascinating extra dimensions to social interaction play, I could definitely see playing characters with an eye to getting deep into that stuff from the outset.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:45:35-07:00","id":905502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905381#post905381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more concerned with Twisted Words Technique, Memory-Reweaving, or similar tricks which bypass (or hijack!) your Intimacies to get right to the mind control -</div> </div> </div> </div> Even if I don't think the result is as bad as you're saying, or the challenge as insurmountable as you think, this seems like an extremely niche kind of problem. I mean, how often are your Solars up against other Solars?<br /> <br /> Or are you modelling all supernatural persuasion powers off of Solar Charms rather than Fakharu's geas or whatever Mara has?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T03:00:40-07:00","id":905511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905501#post905501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bLet me see...<br /> <br /> I think there may be a few things that can get Resolve up to eleven, so can you tell me which one you have in mind so that I can check back on its weaknesses, limitations, or unsustainable costs?</div> </div> </div> </div>The excellency, of course.<br /> <br /> Base pool of 11, divide by 2 for Resolve 6. Spend 10m on the excellency. Don't even have to stunt, though you obviously should.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905501#post905501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I'm reading the Charms, that really does not seem to be the case to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already hard for a mortal to hit the mote-less Resolve of a Solar who invested in Integrity. Spend some motes on the excellency and you can stonewall basically everything. And retrying is hard.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, most people have like 5 dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905501#post905501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But not to the extent of Second Edition, where it was needed to sustain paranoia combos, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sort of. Being willpower-tapped is a lot less bad while it lasts this time around, but it's a lot harder to get willpower back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905501#post905501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, this whole conversation has made me look back over the Integrity Charms, and I'm finding myself perplexed at every statement that Integrity is a soft option for Supernal Ability...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone here said anything like that. You may want to reread the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T03:12:14-07:00","id":905512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905511#post905511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone here said anything like that. You may want to reread the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think he meant in this thread, it is definitely an opinion I have heard (and disagreed with) before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T03:34:27-07:00","id":905524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905511#post905511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The excellency, of course.<br /> <br /> Base pool of 11, divide by 2 for Resolve 6. Spend 10m on the excellency. Don't even have to stunt, though you obviously should.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI suppose that depends on if the specialty applies to the situation.<br /> <br /> But still, if we're talking about the Excellency alone, then we're back in the situation where the cost is unsustainable in the long run. I mean, that's hard enough to do in combat, where you at least have a five mote drip per round. Outside of combat?<br /> <br /> What are you doing after the fourth or fifth time somebody tries to perform a social action against your Essence 1 character? Also, what are you going to do for Charms with your character running on fumes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's already hard for a mortal to hit the mote-less Resolve of a Solar who invested in Integrity. Spend some motes on the excellency and you can stonewall basically everything. And retrying is hard.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, most people have like 5 dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that depends on what kinds of Intimacies you have.<br /> <br /> Like, a Defining Principle of &quot;I keep the innocent from harm&quot; is going to bring that moteless Resolve down to 3 against the Guild factor who uses a Persuade action of &quot;I've made arrangements that will kill half the people in Nexus if you kill me or interfere with my enterprise&quot;, which would have issues even if that's a character with only 5 dice (although for somebody like that it should probably be higher).<br /> <br /> Maybe you can spend Essence to boost your Resolve (like, maybe you'll have enough at the time to do so), but... should you? I mean, even if the player thinks that resisting such a threat is appropriate for the character, and they spend all of that Essence for it and move to kill the factor, what kind of impact is the Excellency going to have in fighting through his badgerfolk bodyguard?<br /> <br /> I think the costs and benefits are reasonably complicated when placed in context.<br /> <br /> Still, depending on the Intimacies.<br /> <br /> (Heh, even assuming a random peasant with a persuade pool of five, against that kind of Principle: &quot;hey, Solar person; your unmitigated rule of us is kind of harmful in a practical sense, do you think you could tone it down a notch?&quot; Even if you use the Excellency to disregard such persuasion outright, what kind of character are you playing?)<br /> <br /> \u200bOh, there's also the concern that, if you're using your Excellency to keep from being persuaded to do something in line with your Intimacies, then that's cause to risk building up Limit, so that's another thing to consider against how hard you want to try to never listen to anybody else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sort of. Being willpower-tapped is a lot less bad while it lasts this time around, but it's a lot harder to get willpower back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Act contrary to your Intimacies for a while. That will get you right back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hey, Segev was right; the Great Curse <i>does</i> entail a measure of temptation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone here said anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Every</b> statement that Integrity is a soft option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-02-2016, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T03:53:42-07:00","id":905528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905524#post905524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI suppose that depends on if the specialty applies to the situation.<br /> <br /> But still, if we're talking about the Excellency alone, then we're back in the situation where the cost is unsustainable in the long run. I mean, that's hard enough to do in combat, where you at least have a five mote drip per round. Outside of combat?<br /> <br /> What are you doing after the fourth or fifth time somebody tries to perform a social action against your Essence 1 character? Also, what are you going to do for Charms with your character running on fumes?</div> </div> </div> </div>This entire conversation is about the dice cap, dude. You said they probably avoided cap-boosters so you couldn't stonewall guildsmen and the like. I'm saying that you can stonewall guildsmen and the like without any cap-boosters, so that's probably not the reason.<br /> <br /> All this stuff about mote costs is totally irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905524#post905524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that depends on what kinds of Intimacies you have.<br /> <br /> Like, a Defining Principle of &quot;I keep the innocent from harm&quot; is going to bring that moteless Resolve down to 3...</div> </div> </div> </div>It does depend.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is off-topic, but I'd expect most people to be rocking a +2 bonus from a Minor Intimacy most of the time. If you don't care at least that much, chances are you don't need to be convinced. And you'll pick up Minor Ties of enmity pretty quickly when meeting people like that hypothetical factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905524#post905524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Heh, even assuming a random peasant with a persuade pool of five...</div> </div> </div> </div>Five dice is for heroes and professionals. Random peasants have maybe two dice.<br /> <br /> This isn't me talking, I'm basically quoting the guidelines at you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905524#post905524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Every</b> statement that Integrity is a soft option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you're getting at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T04:31:33-07:00","id":905542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905528#post905528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This entire conversation is about the dice cap, dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that to mean things that boost the static value without regards to Excellencies. If I am mistaken...<br /> <br /> \u200bDammit it, this is one of those annoying occasions in which I want to sincerely make a request, but I'm absolutely sure every way I could word it will sound snippy and hostile.<br /> <br /> No joking, if I'm incorrect, I would like to know what you mean, so I can better refine my understanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said they probably avoided cap-boosters so you couldn't stonewall guildsmen and the like. I'm saying that you can stonewall guildsmen and the like without any cap-boosters, so that's probably not the reason.<br /> <br /> All this stuff about mote costs is totally irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I think the costs of the Excellency are a significant part of the dynamic of things like the social system; that in practical terms, you can't stonewall everything, so you're going to be a lot more discerning. I think that the things you're saying aren't there, as I understand them (and again, if that is mistaken, I would appreciate a correction) would be things that would make it too easy to ignore the social system.<br /> <br /> That and I'm reading into what is made of the Integrity Charms that we do have; that so many of them provide defences and denials that are conditional in several ways that drive plot hooks or emphasize character traits. That's part of why I think what I do about what they were going for with Solar Integrity engaging with the social system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't care at least that much, chances are you don't need to be convinced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having a hard time reading this... are you saying &quot;if one doesn't care about <u>not</u> doing a thing, then they don't need to be convinced to do it&quot;? As in, if somebody needs to even convince you to go down to the shops to pick up some milk for them, it implies that you have at least a Minor Intimacy towards not going to the shops?<br /> <br /> I don't think that's how persuade actions work; if something in any way represents a change in course or the slightest inconvenience, then the system assumes a character needs to be convinced to do it. Sure, you, as the player, ultimately decide what is and isn't convenient, but not every occasion where they decide that it does not rests on an Intimacy. You can be resistant to doing something on the basis of nothing more than it not being something you were already doing, you don't need a codified conviction against it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Five dice is for heroes and professionals. Random peasants have maybe two dice.<br /> <br /> This isn't me talking, I'm basically quoting the guidelines at you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it does.<br /> <br /> Not random peasant, then, but the nominated spokesperson peasant; the one who's always been the most articulate and good at representing the needs of the community.<br /> <br /> Random peasant needs to spend Willpower and be supremely lucky, which is unlikely, but probably makes for a highly memorable game experience on the occasion when it does happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what you're getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Statements about Integrity as a Supernal Ability have existed outside of this thread.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: As for the topic, another reason that a Solar who has run out of Willpower and invested in Integrity is not completely at the mercy of the Psyche Charms of the other Solar; an early access Charm to substitute motes for the Willpower cost to resist social influence and mind-affecting magic.<br /> <br /> Also, if the cost of Transcendent Hero's Meditation is so offensive, then there's Righteous Soul Judgement to waive it altogether.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-02-2016, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T04:41:00-07:00","id":905545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905381#post905381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real tragedy is the Taste &amp; Smell crowd.<br /> <br /> Sight is amazing - it gets huge dice-trick-boosted schenanigans for Join Battle, opposing Larceny, and beating Stealth. Hearing/Touch is okay - it gets an even stronger trick than Sight, but only against stealth (including Join Battle versus Stealthed enemies). And Taste/Smell gets... a rock. Which is to say, conditional efficiency boosts if they have an Intimacy for a Stealthed person... and nothing else. No cap-breaking (that the other subtrees don't get, too), no reasonably-common cases where they reign supreme, nothing. How big of a deal are those dice tricks? At Essence 5 and against equal opposition, it winds up some 7-11 average successes behind the other senses. Never specialize for Taste/Smell.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as dice tricks and JB goes, yeah, smell and taste sucks. On the other hand, two of its three side branch charms give new capabilities, which is more than you can say about the other senses. Genius Pallet and Foe-Scenting are awesome.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it only has 3 side branch charms, which is quite a bit fewer than the other senses get, which sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:34:05-07:00","id":905618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905545#post905545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as dice tricks and JB goes, yeah, smell and taste sucks. On the other hand, two of its three side branch charms give new capabilities, which is more than you can say about the other senses. Genius Pallet and Foe-Scenting are awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Genius Palate is a cool idea, but... in two decades playing assorted RPGs, I literally cannot come up of an instance when it would have been useful. Ever. The one time in a campaign where someone is eating a meal prepared by a character they wish to learn the emotional state of (who isn't actually present for them to observe), I'd probably allow it as a Stunt - I'd require the Charm to do so reliably, but what's going on that you need this thing reliably?<br /> <br /> (Sure, there's an implication that it auto-detects poisons, but even beyond my issues with unclear implications in Exalted Charms... is that really not something you can do anyway with 9+ dice on an Awareness roll?)<br /> <br /> Foe-Scenting Method is good, though. But good enough to rob yourself of the best Join Battle in the game? At least it's only a two-Charm dip when you're mostly invested in another sense - and you needed one of those two Charms for Eye of the Unconquered Sun, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T08:32:03-07:00","id":905664,"title":"","content":"Depends on how much you care about JB vs new cool stuff you can do. Like I have a character for whom I don't care that much about join battle, so those smell and taste charms are good.<br /> <br /> Of course, I def think there should be more variety and some more general JB boosters, and def that smell/taste just don't have enough going for them.<br /> <br /> Also. On Genius Pallet? Oh man can that be useful. Basically any time you're at a party, or someone buys you a drink at a bar, or in any hospitality situation (which can be extremely common in Creation) you automatically know that their deal is. That's good. I have no idea how you haven't crossed those situations at all ever before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T09:49:28-07:00","id":905726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905664#post905664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also. On Genius Pallet? Oh man can that be useful. Basically any time you're at a party, or someone buys you a drink at a bar, or in any hospitality situation (which can be extremely common in Creation) you automatically know that their deal is. That's good. I have no idea how you haven't crossed those situations at all ever before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've crossed a lot of situations which fit with what you're describing, but don't really reach the Charm's text.<br /> <br /> If someone buys you a drink at a bar, you know <i>what the bartender's deal is.</i> That's kinda interesting, but how often are you interested by the bartender (or the vinter, I guess, if it's not a mixed drink)? And let's say the GM throws in something neat - you learn that the bartender is angry. What then? Are they a member of a secretive cult who plot to overthrow you and the other patrons... or are they just wishing they got better tips? GPS doesn't tell you that. For two motes, you learned that there's an angry bartender. If you'd spent those two motes on an Excellency, you probably could have made a real Read Intentions action, learning either more nuanced information about what they're thinking (&quot;what is their reaction to looking at the host of the party?&quot;), or that they're an exceptionally-skilled liar (when you can easily get 4+ successes, failure can be more revealing than success... assuming you don't auto-succeed). And it gets even less useful when you learn what an unseen cook was feeling hours ago. Even in a hospitality situation, it won't tell you whether overwhelming joy from the farmers taking you in means you've got kind people, or Misery Graves.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Charm! But I'd struggle to justify it as anything other than cool fluff if it were free, Permanent, and explicitly called out that it identifies all ingredients (for both showing off and resolving the poison thing). As-is, I am - as ever! - glad to hear that people are having fun in their games, but it looks super narrow to me. Hum. Maybe an upgrade, to let it pick up on a random Intimacy? That moves its usefulness into the realm of GM fiat (since a &quot;random&quot; intimacy could always be something dull and trivial, even from a personal rival), but makes it a flavorful way to hand off information, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:43:53-07:00","id":905765,"title":"","content":"Get a pitcher of beer, and get someone to pour you a glass. Meet someone for tea, get them to pour you a cup. Get someone to grab a fruit for you. You have shit Socialize? They have Guile 10? Doesn't matter, you auto succeed. It's not a Socialize charm, and that's important. It gives someone in awareness a way to do read intentions well. It's limited in use, but very powerful for what it does. And works on people who otherwise might be extremely difficult to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:45:20-07:00","id":905768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905765#post905765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get a pitcher of beer, and get someone to pour you a glass. Meet someone for tea, get them to pour you a cup. Get someone to grab a fruit for you. You have shit Socialize? They have Guile 10? Doesn't matter, you auto succeed. It's not a Socialize charm, and that's important. It gives someone in awareness a way to do read intentions well. It's limited in use, but very powerful for what it does. And works on people who otherwise might be extremely difficult to read.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Chejop Kejak's love of tea will be his downfall! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:58:55-07:00","id":905774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905768#post905768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chejop Kejak's love of tea will be his downfall! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is true in real life. I have a bookcase full of assorted loose-leaf teas beside my bed, and it's only a matter of time before it falls on my bed and crushes me in my sleep.<br /> <br /> I am still not sold on the utility of learning someone's emotional state, though. It's pretty limited! Still, the point is taken: it's a new capability, Awareness is low on those, and people are inventive at using things. I don't want to rag on that Charm, since my bigger points are (1) Awareness is light on new capabilities, and (2) Smell/Taste is light on meat, period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:24:22-07:00","id":905803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905115#post905115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I find it interesting that the same player base which can complain about Solars always being better than everybody else at everything will also enthusiastically complain about a Solar Charmset that leaves room for other Exalt types to be good at some things in their own ways. Is it perhaps possible that these so-called gaps are not oversights, but the result of a deliberate design decision to define the expression of Solar excellence with regards to the game's Abilities differently than that of other, not-yet-published Exalted?<br /> <br /> Do we really want Solars to stake out <i>all </i>the best design space before anybody else even comes on to the scene?<br /> <br /> Do we <i>really</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't follow in the least. Dragon-Blooded and Lunars aren't going to lack defensive Melee charms simply because Solars have them, nor will they lack Craft charms to assist with making Artifacts within the terminus. That's not how Exalted works.<br /> <br /> You are correct that some gaps are intentional, like the limited defensive options of Brawl. However, Solars aren't going to lack basic functionality in an Ability (particularly in direct application, which are a Solar focus). John's comments regarding the infinite nature of the Solar charm tree, and his decision to drop in 70 more Solar charms is proof of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:31:14-07:00","id":905812,"title":"","content":"Any differences the other splats have to solars will likely be in approach rather than end result.<br /> <br /> The thing about the solar charm set being infinite is that a set can be infinite without including everything.<br /> <br /> Take the real positive integers. There's an infinite number of those. But none of those numbers are -3. In fact the real negative integers form their own infinite set.<br /> <br /> So you have two infinitely large sets with no overlap whatsoever. That's how charms work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T13:01:24-07:00","id":905894,"title":"","content":"From a certain point of view, the answer to the question of wanting Solars to stake out the best design space is... kind of yes.<br /> <br /> In the past, it was for the case of establishing the credibility of Solars as the mightiest of the Exalted, and would be the kind of thing that would diminish over time as developing new Exalted caused the Charm technology to evolve without them. I understand that one of the big complaints about Sidereals was that they had a lot of social effects that the core system had not really accounted for, so it made Solars look weaker both in the sense that their own social options were crude or limited, and they lacked an effective way to preserve themselves in the face of it, neither of which really seem like they would fit the Solar image.<br /> <br /> So in terms of mechanics, one of the things they were going for is trying to draft out how others can work ahead of time so that Solars could be preconceived with ways to interact with them.<br /> <br /> Plus all of those things Totentanz said about how the Solar milieu is encompassing while other groups are weird anyway.<br /> <br /> Like, trying to suss out the logical extent of something like Linguistics Charms, which will even be different for different people (and could be a subject for discussion in a different thread) doesn't exactly extend to how Sidereal Linguistics is the kind of thing that will include magically binding wedding vows.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T20:40:32-07:00","id":906164,"title":"","content":"I'm going to ignore the loud assertions that I am wrong about things I never said because...yeah.<br /> <br /> Instead, let us consider the possibility that Solar essence expresses itself in particular ways that can be <i>unsurpassed </i>without being <i>all-encompassing</i>. Brawl was mentioned and is a good example. The Solar Brawler is nigh-unapproachable in expressing raw physical violence. By such a measure he is unequivocally the best - even if there are certain smaller component aspects of combat that do not find expression in the Charm set! Does this mean that no other character type is allowed to explore that space in their Brawl tree? No, of course not. And in fact this is a good thing, because it allows Brawl to be explored in distinctive ways by other Exalts without threatening the supremacy of the Solar as king of the ring. He can beat up anybody, even if he doesn't know every conceivable move. He is <i>the best </i>but can still be bounded by the ways in which his essence naturally expresses itself.<br /> <br /> Now consider a hypothetical case: War. I have seen more than a few complaints that War offers great options at the strategic level but few (or no) options at the small-group or Circle level. Leave aside the fact that Battle Group rules kick in at three Followers for the moment and let's simply take this observation at face value for the sake of argument. It is typically presented as somehow evidence of a shortcoming in the tree, i.e. &quot;I can command an army but not an elite team of dudes, wtf devs?!&quot;. But...is it an oversight? Or is it <i>perhaps </i>instead an implicit statement to the effect that the essence of the greatest God of War in Heaven, when wielded by his Chosen, simply <i>doesn't do the small stuff</i>. After all, Solars were raised up to be generals, not sergeants. What if Solars don't have small-unit tactics Charms because they're <i>not supposed to</i>. They are supposed to lead <i>armies</i>, not individual units, and their essence swells and expands to find expression at the grander scale rather than the lesser. This in no way makes them weaker - it reinforces the massive scale that such world-shaking heroes are supposed to operate at. If a Solar wants to beat the crap out of his enemies, he can either bring a mighty host against them or he can <i>personally </i>kick their asses straight to hell. The fact that his essence doesn't lend itself to small-scale teamwork may be simply...irrelevant. I can think of other Exalted who were intended to operate well at such scales, however, and I bet <i>you </i>can too.<br /> <br /> The Solars can be <i>the best and the brightest and the strongest </i>without necessarily being kitchen-sink repositories of every conceivable take on a given Ability. And I would argue that the game is <i>better </i>if this is the case. Not everyone will agree, I know. At some places and times the game has interpreted the nature of Solar essence as &quot;unlimited&quot; to apply not just to puissance but also to comprehensive breadth of potential, and some folks will be very invested in retaining this. I think it's worth considering the possibility that 3E might not be making that assumption. The Unconquered Sun is, after all, unsurpassed without being infinitely plastic in his power. Why would his Chosen be otherwise?<br /> <br /> I don't know if this is definitively the case, and I don't claim to. But perhaps Solars don't have to be <i>capable of anything </i>to be <i>the best at everything</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T20:45:34-07:00","id":906168,"title":"","content":"Also I just have to respond to this because seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905803#post905803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">basic functionality</div> </div> </div> </div>Wut? Excellencies, bro. <i>Come on</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T21:21:57-07:00","id":906187,"title":"","content":"I don't think Solars need to be capable of <i>literally</i> anything, but I do think Solars should (at least theoretically) be capable of <i>anything that a human can do skillfully</i>. Solars are supposed to &quot;express the totality of human excellence.&quot;<br /> <br /> I could understand why the War Charms actually printed within the corebook's wordcount limit don't focus on small unit tactics, but it would be very silly for Solars to be unable to express Charms relating to small unit tactics at all. Especially since one of the big themes Solars have, aside from &quot;excellence,&quot; is &quot;leadership.&quot; Do you really think it would be out of theme for a Night Caste to lead an elite commando unit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906164#post906164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun is, after all, unsurpassed without being infinitely plastic in his power. Why would his Chosen be otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they were made to do a job of which he was totally incapable...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T22:23:52-07:00","id":906213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905542#post905542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that to mean things that boost the static value without regards to Excellencies. If I am mistaken...<br /> <br /> \u200bDammit it, this is one of those annoying occasions in which I want to sincerely make a request, but I'm absolutely sure every way I could word it will sound snippy and hostile.<br /> <br /> No joking, if I'm incorrect, I would like to know what you mean, so I can better refine my understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kejak talked about the lack of Resolve cap-breakers. You said they probably avoided them to keep people from stonewalling mortal social influence. I said no, you don't need cap-breakers to do that. A Permanent Charm that added 1000000000000000000000 to your Resolve cap would have basically no effect on your ability to stall guildsmen.<br /> <br /> Far as I'm concerned, the rest of this conversation is a tangent to a tangent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905542#post905542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a hard time reading this... are you saying &quot;if one doesn't care about <u>not</u> doing a thing, then they don't need to be convinced to do it&quot;? As in, if somebody needs to even convince you to go down to the shops to pick up some milk for them, it implies that you have at least a Minor Intimacy towards not going to the shops?<br /> <br /> I don't think that's how persuade actions work; if something in any way represents a change in course or the slightest inconvenience, then the system assumes a character needs to be convinced to do it. Sure, you, as the player, ultimately decide what is and isn't convenient, but not every occasion where they decide that it does not rests on an Intimacy. You can be resistant to doing something on the basis of nothing more than it not being something you were already doing, you don't need a codified conviction against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But I think when people bring out the dice at the table, people's convictions are gonna be involved a strong majority of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905542#post905542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Statements about Integrity as a Supernal Ability have existed outside of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I missed those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T03:16:34-07:00","id":906295,"title":"","content":"I explained what I thought &quot;cap breaker&quot; meant, and how that assumption formed the basis of my response. If what I thought the term meant was incorrect, I have no idea, since I can't get a straight answer.<br /> <br /> And I am continuously disagreeing with and presenting arguments against the assertion that the Excellency represents a meaningful bypass of the social influence system, as pertinent to <b>any</b> characters who might try to influence players.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T03:57:59-07:00","id":906309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906295#post906295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I explained what I thought &quot;cap breaker&quot; meant, and how that assumption formed the basis of my response. If what I thought the term meant was incorrect, I have no idea, since I can't get a straight answer.<br /> <br /> And I am continuously disagreeing with and presenting arguments against the assertion that the Excellency represents a meaningful bypass of the social influence system, as pertinent to <b>any</b> characters who might try to influence players.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Cap breakers is something which allow you to get a higher (average) result than merely using a full excellency, such as non-charm dice, or double X effects.<br /> The name comes from how such effects &quot;break&quot; the dice cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/613-vegetalss4","name":"Vegetalss4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar613_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T07:58:33-07:00","id":906413,"title":"","content":"All right, so having looked back over the Dodge Charms myself and seeing that the one being used as an example of a cap-booster is the very first Charm, I see how the term is being applied, and I believe I can refine my point.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, I see three points of comparison between a cap-booster for Evasion and one for Resolve.<br /> <br /> 1) Evasion is used in combat, meaning that matters of efficiency in spending even more motes are partially offset by the constant mote drip; combat in general can be easier on Essence concerns, since it's a high stakes scenario that encourages big investments for big returns.<br /> <br /> 2) The effects of being hit with something that you would Evade can be a lot more granular and dramatic than social influence or Psyche effects, which tend to be mechanically binary and easier to recover from. You'll more likely have a scenario in which an opposing dice pool is high enough, which can create a more severe effect upon success, that increasing the difficulty of that dice roll will feel a lot more warranted.<br /> <br /> 3) While Dodge Charms help add a lot more nuance to the gameplay of evading in combat, the actual act of dodging itself is not very narratively invested.<br /> <br /> That last one is something I see as particularly pertinent, looking at the Integrity Charms we got, and indeed, the Psyche Charms we got, because I find that the thing they were often going for there was to make the process of preserving your will or shaking of mind control more a series of actions or relationships, rather than always boiling down to just spending something to unilaterally shut something down. <br /> <br /> So even if you have no Integrity Charms, something like Memory-Reweaving Discipline has an in-built story process for somebody shaking off having their memories altered, and if they're using the Integrity Charms designed for shaking off such effects, those also portray an action or process to doing so based on things like who the character is or what they have seen, rather than it just being switched off.<br /> <br /> That and how Psyche effects are less common than their prior Editions' counterparts and are, if not narrow, then at least intricate in their procedures, so having your mind affected can rarely be character destroying. Even if one was going to present a power that did control more thoroughly, I would say that the precedents given show that they should be designed to include interesting plot hooks around their methods of resistance.<br /> <br /> I mean, that was all something that I didn't like in Second Edition; you come up with all kinds of interesting powers to affect the mind, and the only necessary response to them is to spend one to three Willpower. It was <i>worse</i> then cheap perfect defences, because even if those were terrible for cutting the teeth from your cool attacks, at least the only things attacks could do was kill you; mind powers create entire new courses of plot, except they don't, because the method of stopping them is boring and people aren't likely to let them play out for its relative cheapness.<br /> <br /> This is also why I like how they made responses to things like deleterious transformations and curses into potentially useful new traits or ongoing plot hooks.<br /> <br /> And it's all packaged in the context of how social actions or Psyche effects are most likely taking place in low-stress, low-stakes environments, which not only shapes concerns over their success, but also the frequency with which they might be deployed and concerns over how draining it is to resist them. Even if, on occasions where you absolutely, positively don't want a social action or Psyche effect to so much as succeed, your natural Resolve cap will probably be good enough anyway.<br /> <br /> Really, to expand on the point about the narrative investment of Dodging, that's another thing that shows how the Abilities are operating in different contexts that suggest different Charms; the narrative process of surviving through a fight consists of all of the actions you take during the fight, and all of the ways that opposing actions constrain and move you even when they don't succeed. No attack will hit you if you use Seven Shadow Evasion, but the conditions of that Charm will then shape the next several rounds of the fight. Things that are not fights are not so intricate, so other avenues have to be taken to make action and reaction into an interesting story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:18:59-07:00","id":906423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vegetalss4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906309#post906309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cap breakers is something which allow you to get a higher (average) result than merely using a full excellency, such as non-charm dice, or double X effects.<br /> The name comes from how such effects &quot;break&quot; the dice cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm... no. A cap breaker is something that allows you to increase your dice by more than the maximum of ability + attribute you are normally allowed. Non-charm dice yes, double X no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:49:04-07:00","id":906442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906295#post906295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I explained what I thought &quot;cap breaker&quot; meant, and how that assumption formed the basis of my response. If what I thought the term meant was incorrect, I have no idea, since I can't get a straight answer.<br /> <br /> And I am continuously disagreeing with and presenting arguments against the assertion that the Excellency represents a meaningful bypass of the social influence system, as pertinent to <b>any</b> characters who might try to influence players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I thought that bit was well-understood. A cap-breaker is something which breaks the cap. Is that clear enough?<br /> <br /> I suggest waiting for someone to make that assertion before presenting arguments against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T13:40:19-07:00","id":906677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906423#post906423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhm... no. A cap breaker is something that allows you to increase your dice by more than the maximum of ability + attribute you are normally allowed. Non-charm dice yes, double X no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I use &quot;cap-breaker&quot; to refer to doubles, rerolls, subtracting enemy successes, and everything else which gives you a better chance of victory than a full Excellency.<br /> <br /> This is because I am a dreary person who sees dice as probability.<br /> <br /> I know it's a bit controversial, and so I've hesitated to mention it, but the game does conspiciously lack Medicine Charms for helping more than just the patient in front of you. No Charms for devising cures, recommending an efficacious program of health and exercise, making the area around you especially hostile to diseases, etc. Yes, this is deliberate. But coming from a splat full of Old Testament references who can nourish followers with their ideals alone, lead prayers which keep the raw tides of Chaos at bay, and and train crowds of laypeople into world-class experts in weeks, it seems really odd to be so stymied by germs*. Helping others and applying personal efforts across implausible scales are core Solar themes, right? Certainly, it seems odd to me that the best Solar Charm for fighting a plague is Favor-Conferring Prana (to set up multiple doctors each capable of providing treatments, since the Ultimate Solar Doctor can still only treat twenty people per day, tops).<br /> <br /> <br /> * I do not know whether Creation has actual literal germs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:09:04-07:00","id":906697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906442#post906442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I suggest waiting for someone to make that assertion before presenting arguments against it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I am \u200bdisagreeing and arguing against the idea that the Excellency allows one to effectively stonewall influence in a manner that suggests that the Integrity Charms do not have a priority in avoiding such effects, then.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T15:38:19-07:00","id":906757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906677#post906677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly, it seems odd to me that the best Solar Charm for fighting a plague is Favor-Conferring Prana (to set up multiple doctors each capable of providing treatments, since the Ultimate Solar Doctor can still only treat twenty people per day, tops).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the best Charm for fighting a plague is <i>First Knowledge's Grace </i>and the other teaching Charms, which will allow you to train mortal physicians. Or perhaps <i>Underling-Promoting Touch </i>to bestow authority upon local community leaders to facilitate quarantine procedures and effective corpse disposal. And then <i>Speed the Wheels </i>to make the city's ailing bureaucracy enact a public-health-crisis plan in a day instead of a season.<br /> <br /> The game neither encourages nor facilitates solutions that amount to &quot;I wave my arms and spend some essence to personally cure all the sick people in this city, story over, let's go get pizza&quot;. Thank goodness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T15:45:24-07:00","id":906762,"title":"","content":"As an aside, I suddenly have a powerful urge to write up Solar <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florence_Nightingale\" target=\"_blank\">Florence Nightingale</a>. God damn she'd be the best Twilight <i>ever</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:08:35-07:00","id":906773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906757#post906757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game neither encourages nor facilitates solutions that amount to &quot;I wave my arms and spend some essence to personally cure all the sick people in this city, story over, let's go get pizza&quot;. Thank goodness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know a lot of people love that.<br /> <br /> It just seems arbitrary to me, given how many serious historical issues there are that Solars CAN wave their arms and burn Essence to deal with. Once again, they can answer a famine by <i>preaching so well that people don't need to eat</i>. They can punch out many natural disasters. They can reliably talk down angry mobs. Leaving combat out of it, that's a TON of things which would (1) be a high barrier to any real-world state, and (2) would probably mostly involve punching out an evil Wizard in D&amp;D*. Solars get to deal with them through their signature mix of pulp heroics and Dragon Ball Z.<br /> <br /> But not diseases. This confuses me.<br /> <br /> <br /> * I'm referencing what Lea's said in the past, obviously, but I feel I should be clear: I've never played a D&amp;D adventure where you punch an evil wizard to stop a plague, but I've totally played a Pathfinder adventure where some evil magicey people are spreading a plague, and the solution is to protect the experts working on a cure whilst also tracking down the conspiracy so they'll stop introducing more. Exalted, meanwhile, prominently features a magical plague made by an evil wizard which was only stopped when an adventuring party successfully completed an ancient castle full of deathtraps. Something worth considering next time we get the old &quot;bash D&amp;D&quot; meme rolling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:22:07-07:00","id":906777,"title":"","content":"I think a Solar giving speeches is useful for when you're leading them through the desert for forty years, but less sustainable if everybody is settled and widespread and possibly where the major issue is poverty rather than scarcity.<br /> <br /> \u200bTalking down angry mobs is something that still engages with the social system, as well as what it implies about people; there's a point at which not redressing <i>why</i> people are angry will mean they don't really listen to the Solar anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:23:00-07:00","id":906779,"title":"","content":"Another gap nobody's mentioned yet - Athletics has no enhancements (apart from the Excellency/God Body) for opposing a disengage action. The only options are in MA, in two different form charms (one of which gets shrugged off with Willpower).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5411-andrewh","name":"AndrewH","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:25:45-07:00","id":906781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906677#post906677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's a bit controversial, and so I've hesitated to mention it, but the game does conspiciously lack Medicine Charms for helping more than just the patient in front of you. No Charms for devising cures, recommending an efficacious program of health and exercise, making the area around you especially hostile to diseases, etc. Yes, this is deliberate. But coming from a splat full of Old Testament references who can nourish followers with their ideals alone, lead prayers which keep the raw tides of Chaos at bay, and and train crowds of laypeople into world-class experts in weeks, it seems really odd to be so stymied by germs*. Helping others and applying personal efforts across implausible scales are core Solar themes, right? Certainly, it seems odd to me that the best Solar Charm for fighting a plague is Favor-Conferring Prana (to set up multiple doctors each capable of providing treatments, since the Ultimate Solar Doctor can still only treat twenty people per day, tops).</div> </div> </div> </div>You might like my next batch of homebrew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906697#post906697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am \u200bdisagreeing and arguing against the idea that the Excellency allows one to effectively stonewall influence in a manner that suggests that the Integrity Charms do not have a priority in avoiding such effects, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone here has claimed that Integrity Charms don't have a priority in avoiding mental influence. Assuming &quot;have a priority&quot; means what I think it does.<br /> <br /> So if you want to argue that, you might have to go elsewhere to find someone willing to take up the other side of the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:28:50-07:00","id":906784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AndrewH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906779#post906779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another gap nobody's mentioned yet - Athletics has no enhancements (apart from the Excellency/God Body) for opposing a disengage action. The only options are in MA, in two different form charms (one of which gets shrugged off with Willpower).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/865075-ranged-combat-rules-blues\">That's intentional, apparently.</a> At least for the similar situation regarding rushes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:29:13-07:00","id":906785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AndrewH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906779#post906779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another gap nobody's mentioned yet - Athletics has no enhancements (apart from the Excellency/God Body) for opposing a disengage action. The only options are in MA, in two different form charms (one of which gets shrugged off with Willpower).</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that's not so much a Charm gap as rules changes.<br /> <br /> The &quot;running&quot; Athletics Charms talk a lot about &quot;Tests of Speed,&quot; which seem to have been some sort of Extended Action, but are not otherwise attested in the rules. And then, as you say, they don't talk about being used to oppose Disengage, even though that's an Athletics roll. I suspect that at some point, there was a whole subsystem here, but it eventually got cut, with parts of it becoming Rush and Disengage, and other parts disappearing.<br /> <br /> Even still, I'd be hesitant to just let a player use their Rush Charms to oppose Disengage checks - Rush can be so much better than Disengage already, making it even stronger seems awfully harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:41:29-07:00","id":906801,"title":"","content":"Allow me to disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906773#post906773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they can answer a famine by <i>preaching so well that people don't need to eat</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they can't. Not really. They can feed people so long as they continue preaching at them, but that doesn't solve a famine because <i>there's still no food</i>. The Solar can keep a group of people from starving to death as long as they hear his words, but as soon as he moves on they are just as screwed as they were before unless he actually takes steps to address the larger problem. There is no Charm for that, and rightly so.<br /> <br /> But that all ignores the more important fact that leading your loyal followers through the desert, nourished by your words, is simply <i>a different story</i> from curing a city of the plague. They are narratively dissimilar in many ways, and what is appropriate for one is not necessarily appropriate for the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can punch out many natural disasters. </div> </div> </div>How? I'll be honest, I missed the Charms that let Solars sucker-punch hurricanes and uppercut forest-fires. I'd, uh, like to know where those are. Seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can reliably talk down angry mobs. </div> </div> </div>Regular people can do that <i>without </i>Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:53:42-07:00","id":906807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906785#post906785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;running&quot; Athletics Charms talk a lot about &quot;Tests of Speed,&quot; which seem to have been some sort of Extended Action, but are not otherwise attested in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's &quot;test of speed&quot; not &quot;Tests of Speed.&quot; It's just a phrase, not a rules term. The first instance of the phrase in the Athletics section refers you back to the page on extended rolls (because that's what tests of speed will most often be), which even gives an example of a foot race. The phrase &quot;test of speed&quot; is used a lot in the Athletics Charms because a lot of Athletics Charms benefit you when you're trying to go quick, and &quot;test of speed&quot; is a relatively succinct phrase that envelops any kind of movement (climbing, swimming, jumping between rocks) for which you're trying to do something faster than someone or something else..<br /> <br /> I realize how it happened, but I never took that phrase to mean anything more than it is, and until I heard other people talking about it how you do, CK, I never would've realized there was this idea it used to be some special rule or something. A totally weird reading to my eyes.<br /> <br /> I always suspected, and Sanct has a link to prove it, that there aren't Athletics Charms to benefit opposing Disengages because the devs wanted to push combat to be more dynamic, not have everyone get stuck around the one guy who can hold them all in place with big charm-powered rolls.<br /> <br /> That said, I think there's space for limited use Charms that benefit opposing disengage. Like a once-per-scene reroll or something as you trip someone up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:07:03-07:00","id":906816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906781#post906781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone here has claimed that Integrity Charms don't have a priority in avoiding mental influence. Assuming &quot;have a priority&quot; means what I think it does.<br /> <br /> So if you want to argue that, you might have to go elsewhere to find someone willing to take up the other side of the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you know how you responded to my first suggestion of why Integrity Charms don't have Resolve cap-boosters? All that stuff about how I was incorrect because of how the Excellency can still boost Resolve?<br /> <br /> However you want to describe your own posts, they're what I am trying to argue against.<br /> <br /> Trying, despite the difficulty of having a conversation with somebody who will introduce the premise that the Integrity Excellency is very significant, and then responds to every attempt to suggest that it is inefficient in the close long term with &quot;Excellencies don't matter to this discussion&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: I am not being gaslighted. I am not being gslighted. I am not gbeing haslighted. I am anann not being gaslighted. I am not being gaslighted. I am <b>not</b> being gaslighted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-03-2016, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:25:22-07:00","id":906830,"title":"","content":"You're right, you're not being gaslighted. You're just not getting what I'm trying to say.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's my fault. I'll try to make it clearer:<br /> <br /> The specific reason you suggested for cap-boosters to not exist is not a plausible reason for cap-boosters to not exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:35:13-07:00","id":906833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906807#post906807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always suspected, and Sanct has a link to prove it, that there aren't Athletics Charms to benefit opposing Disengages because the devs wanted to push combat to be more dynamic, not have everyone get stuck around the one guy who can hold them all in place with big charm-powered rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can still do it to some extent through knockdown and grapples. I was looking at making a high-resistance character, who could stand in the middle of a burning raptor, and hold bad guys heads in the fire. Ended up going the knock-down route, which happily had its most effective charm in Tiger Style, which also gives me disengage penalties with the form charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5411-andrewh","name":"AndrewH","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:19:29-07:00","id":906863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906830#post906830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, you're not being gaslighted. You're just not getting what I'm trying to say.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's my fault. I'll try to make it clearer:<br /> <br /> The specific reason you suggested for cap-boosters to not exist is not a plausible reason for cap-boosters to not exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding on this a little: let's do a very coarse-grained division of all of our possible opponents into two groups, which we will call &quot;Mortal die pools&quot; and &quot;Above mortal die pools.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you are a Solar who has invested in his Resolve at all - like, even just raised the mundane stats - you are mostly okay against people with mortal die pools. This is because (a) most of the people with mortal die pools are mortals, who mostly throw, like, 5 dice, (b) even for people throwing 10ish dice, Intimacies <i>tend to</i> favor the defender (because you more rarely need to be convinced to do something that's in line with your character concept anyway), (c) if someone's throwing mortal die pools at you, they're probably also using mundane influence that you can disregard for a Willpower, and (d) if you're really worried, you can always spend a 4-6m on the Excellency to cut their odds down to low-single digits; thanks to the Retrying Social Influence rules on p. 222, they can't spam persuasion attempts, and so this is probably not a repeated expense.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Above mortal die pool&quot; group is much scarier. A social-specced Exalt might be able to average successes on the order of 2x your base Resolve - Lunars, Sidereals, and Dragon-Blooded, at least, can all manage this trick, and E4+ spirits seem to have comparable Excellency-equivalents. And that's if you're <i>also</i> Resolve-focused; if you're rocking 3-4 in the relevant stats, you're in considerably more trouble, and your Excellency cap is lower to boot. Added to that, magic is more likely to be able to ignore your Intimacies, it's often more expensive to resist, and if you <i>don't</i> resist, it can very plausibly wreck your day.<br /> <br /> So it's this second group that's the major concern. And for the second group, the Excellency alone is <i>not likely to suffice</i>; if you have an attacker and a defender with equivalent pools and equivalent Excellencies, odds favor the attacker. That's a big deal! Now, the defender might gain <i>mitigation</i> techniques - ways to recover from being mind-whammied with social magic - but in the Solar combat trees, he also has access to <i>prevention</i> magic that kicks his natural defenses higher than he can get them with Excellencies alone. In Integrity, he doesn't.<br /> <br /> So &quot;But cheaper Excellencies!&quot; - and the Excellency conversation in general - are important for the &quot;Mortal die pool&quot; crowd, but that's not really <i>as major</i> of a concern. By contrast, they're not really a lot of assurance against the really dangerous social characters, and it seems, at least on the face of it, a bit odd that Integrity doesn't get more toys to use to protect yourself.<br /> <br /> (Sanctaphrax, is that roughly fair to your position?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T20:41:00-07:00","id":906921,"title":"","content":"Im not sure i get the comments about lore or survival. I know that there are way more familiar charms then there are wilderness survival charms, but I cant think of any wilderness survival affects that aren't already covered except for maybe shelter for large numbers of people. Same thing with the lore fact charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T21:28:23-07:00","id":906948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906863#post906863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Sanctaphrax, is that roughly fair to your position?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. I do believe most of that stuff. But I didn't really want to mention all those details. I was just trying to say that boosting your Resolve cap has no effect on your interactions with mortals.<br /> <br /> Though I haven't gone deep into the social system, I strongly suspect the key to keeping your mind intact is Spirit-Maintaining Maneuver. Maybe with Undying Solar Resolve. Tanking social influence, so to speak, seems more efficient than trying to block it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T22:58:56-07:00","id":906985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906863#post906863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So &quot;But cheaper Excellencies!&quot; - and the Excellency conversation in general - are important for the &quot;Mortal die pool&quot; crowd, but that's not really <i>as major</i> of a concern. By contrast, they're not really a lot of assurance against the really dangerous social characters, and it seems, at least on the face of it, a bit odd that Integrity doesn't get more toys to use to protect yourself.<br /> <br /> (Sanctaphrax, is that roughly fair to your position?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not Sanctaphrax*, but this is exactly what I meant when I brought this up as a &quot;hole&quot;.<br /> <br /> Solar Integrity defenses overwhelming protect your Intimacies, and mean social BS overwhelmingly bypasses them.<br /> <br /> Though I am now wondering whether something like Twisted Words Technique is a &quot;Not-a-Shaping-Effect&quot; for the pusposes of the Charms which nope out of those. If so, then there is one line of defense, though admittedly a retro one.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Nobody is. It's in his sig, and everything!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T00:29:25-07:00","id":907014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906801#post906801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regular people can do that <i>without </i>Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The comment you quoted contains the word &quot;reliably&quot; - so no, no they can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T08:40:57-07:00","id":907653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904449#post904449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SWAT teams working together seem very Dragonblooded. Solars are more Die Hard, one man army type.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904489#post904489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a bit silly to assert that any one group has more of a lock on the &quot;fight as a group thing&quot; than any other, considering that this is a game for 2-6 players. Is &quot;one man army&quot; really much better than &quot;guards a territory and drives everybody away from it&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904503#post904503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Solars fight in a group more like the Avengers. They each have their own strengths and usually fight their enemies one on one, even if they are all in the same fight. Occasionally they will combo powers (like Hawkeye shooting Ant-Man) but that is rare. Dragonblooded always work together. Hell, maybe they will be able to combo different charms with other Dragonblooded. Who knows?<br /> <br /> Anywho, I tend to consider &quot;Dragonblooded build groups&quot; while, if I remember correctly, you disagreed with that assertion, so this may be one of those &quot;Agree to disagree&quot; topics.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=904516#post904516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holden has repeatedly said that playing combat as everybody dividing one on one is a fool's game, and I see several areas in the system around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Random page 2 necromancy!: My take on this is with both to a degree. Of course, with Isator's point, group dynamics matter for all, because it's a team game.<br /> <br /> However, it means something for an Exalt to have Castes, with a combat Caste, or alternatively to have Aspects, with no combat Aspect. If you have a combat Caste, then in combat the theme is that they take point and everyone else follows and supports. With Aspects, a small group of diverse individuals who express part of what it is to be a warrior to the fullest combine district skills. While this can be modified by situation (e.g. the Dawn is inexperienced vs an experienced rest of part, multiple Dawns in a team, different degrees of specialisation into combat by different Dragonblooded), the designs *do* point to different dynamics. Solars Castes do push more to &quot;Buffy + guys who are helping Buffy&quot; and not &quot;Team of equals&quot; so much. Especially in 3e with Supernal Abilities and revamped Caste Animas.<br /> <br /> (Sidereals seem a bit are intermediate here, and properly, so are Alchemicals and Infernals. With Lunars you probably tend to have more than one Full Moon on a team, if you're playing a game of five, so...).<br /> <br /> I guess I could say this fits with Solar vs Terrestrial mythology - the sun is singular and above, each phase stands alone and dominant in its time, passing over authority to next in their time, the elements combine to be greater than their parts.<br /> <br /> There's a different play experience for each. The Caste social structures of the Solars represent only one possible model and perspective of a heroic team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T09:23:46-07:00","id":907671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905384#post905384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I don't think it's healthy to define yourself like that. Don't be a booster or a hater, just be a person with opinions that are mostly positive or negative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, I have mostly positive opinions of EX3, it's just that things like this are the primary reason I dropped from the playtest (i.e. taste difference so extreme that I could no longer be an impartial or unbiased tester). That being said, I feel the contributions of having a stable development team with a singular vision, even if it's one I don't agree with is more valuable than my distaste for some of resultant design choices. Overall for me it's a question of maintaining positivity in the face of the singular problem which made me leave the PT, hence my more mixed commentary introduction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T09:28:04-07:00","id":907673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=907653#post907653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it means something for an Exalt to have Castes, with a combat Caste, or alternatively to have Aspects, with no combat Aspect. If you have a combat Caste, then in combat the theme is that they take point and everyone else follows and supports. With Aspects, a small group of diverse individuals who express part of what it is to be a warrior to the fullest combine district skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if that's specific to Aspects as a concept instead of just how Abilities are distributed for Dragon Blooded, but it's a good underlying point.<br /> <br /> It may be that Dragon Blooded fighting Charms might follow similar trajectories to those Brawl Charms, with a wide distribution of organic benefits to hitting an enemy before or after an ally. Perhaps that could also lend itself to the image of Dragon Blooded being the weakest while still letting a manageable number of them represent a challenge for players, or being challenging for powerful antagonists when Terrestrials are being played.<br /> <br /> Things that could make the Dragon Blooded play differently from Solars in a manner that emphasizes them all being some kind of warrior, which belies how they can't expand vertically in that area from the outset the way that a Solar can.<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder what Terrestrial Essence progression might be, and how that might play into how their Charm cascades are structured. Perhaps a sense of it being a bit more bottom heavy, along with any group synergies, and maybe any given Essence 5 Charms represent a significant, if limited, boost.<br /> <br /> Heh, Supernal does represent an interesting modification of the usual idea of a &quot;combat focused&quot; character, doesn't it? Like, Prince Diamond is a swordsman by trade and inclination, and yet he's still generally going to be limited to Melee Charms within his Essence level.<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if a Terrestrial who is focused on Melee might be a bit stronger than a Solar who is focused on Melee while they're both at Essence 1, except where the Solar's Charms are still good enough to be competitive; the idea that the Solar who invests about as heavily into a combat Ability as their Essence allows may be at a disadvantage against another Exalt doing something similar, but the disadvantage is not insurmountable, especially with brief bursts of the Excellency.<br /> <br /> Or maybe not quite that extreme, but I think it's an interesting line of thought to pursue.<br /> <br /> It will be interesting to see.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T09:53:30-07:00","id":907691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906985#post906985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> mean social BS</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI still think that begs the question of how likely one is to encounter Psyche effects either used by Solars, or modelled off of what they use, as opposed to things like Fakharu's geas.<br /> <br /> I sometimes think that some people take a bit of a Dick Cheney approach to roleplaying game mechanics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:56:36-07:00","id":907852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=907691#post907691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI still think that begs the question of how likely one is to encounter Psyche effects either used by Solars, or modelled off of what they use, as opposed to things like Fakharu's geas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you not moderately-regularly bump into Celestial Exalts with differing agendas, when you play Exalted? Because that's been a staple of just about every Exalted game I've played.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:10:39-07:00","id":907866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=907852#post907852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you not moderately-regularly bump into Celestial Exalts with differing agendas, when you play Exalted? Because that's been a staple of just about every Exalted game I've played.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention Sorcerers, even mortal ones. In my rewrite I already dealt with Peacock Shadow Eyes and Droning Suggestion, next is Curse of Slavish Humility...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:15:50-07:00","id":907869,"title":"","content":"Corrupted Words is nasty too. Willpower does nothing, so unless you know Transcendent Hero's Meditation or Invincible Solar Aegis you're 100% reliant on Resolve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:21:46-07:00","id":907880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=906168#post906168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I just have to respond to this because seriously.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wut? Excellencies, bro. <i>Come on</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an entire thread full of noted gaps, with a fair group of people agreeing on it. I'd suggest you actually try reading that thread, rather than parachuting in while spraying condescension all over the place. You might be surprised at the results!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:30:20-07:00","id":907929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you not moderately-regularly bump into Celestial Exalts with differing agendas, when you play Exalted? Because that's been a staple of just about every Exalted game I've played.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do we think that Lunars and Sidereals are going to have comparable Psyche effects? Hell, even by those standards, I think a game that relies on them so heavily that being affected by whatever Psyche effects are there or may come is really underselling all other forms of opposition that might come against players; gods, Fair Folk, ninja squads, the giants of Dis...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:53:02-07:00","id":907943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=907929#post907929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do we think that Lunars and Sidereals are going to have comparable Psyche effects? Hell, even by those standards, I think a game that relies on them so heavily that being affected by whatever Psyche effects are there or may come is really underselling all other forms of opposition that might come against players; gods, Fair Folk, ninja squads, the giants of Dis...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm pretty sure people are underselling fact that one Fiend encounter can probably ruin entire Circle and end in TPK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:07:37-07:00","id":907988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=907929#post907929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do we think that Lunars and Sidereals are going to have comparable Psyche effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect they're going to have pretty nasty ones, yeah. I mean, I feel like the odds of the Sidereals having some kind of horrible sideways-logic mind-control effects are somewhere between &quot;Yes&quot; and &quot;Obviously yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Having answered your question, would you answer mine? Have you played many games that didn't run into Celestial-tier social opposition?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, even by those standards, I think a game that relies on them so heavily that being affected by whatever Psyche effects are there or may come is really underselling all other forms of opposition that might come against players; gods, Fair Folk, ninja squads, the giants of Dis... </div> </div> </div>That's a separate conversation. Let's stay on the topic of angry social Celestials and how one mechanically opposes them in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T02:32:49-07:00","id":908214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=905803#post905803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't follow in the least. Dragon-Blooded and Lunars aren't going to lack defensive Melee charms simply because Solars have them, nor will they lack Craft charms to assist with making Artifacts within the terminus. That's not how Exalted works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean, I do expect Lunars to be fairly lacking on the Craft front, but that's less because Solars have it and more because Lunars have had practically fuck all to help with artifacts for two editions running, and the fact that devs supposedly want to focus on the physical and barbarian rebel parts of their fluff doesn't seem a thing that would point to the streak being broken being the most likely of things :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 06-06-2016, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:01:55-07:00","id":908219,"title":"","content":"I think it's more the fact that they just don't have ability charms.<br /> <br /> I actually do think Lunars will get a few Craft charms (or rather, Intelligence charms that help with Crafting, though they might not only help with Crafting), but not many.<br /> <br /> So, I've just got into this conversation, and reading back I'm not completely up on what Isator and Irked are arguing about. So I just want to make sure I understand people's positions before diving in?<br /> <br /> Irked, are you saying Solars lack ways to reliably defend against mind-control and other very serious social attacks, whereas they do have ways to reliably defend against physical attacks (even if those cost a lot, but that's not the point)? That all they can do is boost their Resolve up to 10 (11 with a spec)?<br /> (I get the point about how making excellencies cheaper doesn't help with this, or other charms that increase your Resolve for cheap, like Elusive Dreams Defence or Temptating-Resisting Stance, since you can still only increase your Resolve by 5, but that's a seperate point)<br /> <br /> Isator, you're saying you don't think it's not a big deal because you don't think Solars are going to be attacked by such effects very often?<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's this second group that's the major concern. And for the second group, the Excellency alone is <i>not likely to suffice</i>; if you have an attacker and a defender with equivalent pools and equivalent Excellencies, odds favor the attacker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the favourability only slight though? I mean, if I have 21 dice and you have Resolve 11 (max pools) then I only have a very slight advantage over you, statistically.<br /> (I think, I haven't run the exact probability)<br /> I mean, you are right, but as far as I see it's a pretty small advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:32:25-07:00","id":908231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=908219#post908219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isator, you're saying you don't think it's not a big deal because you don't think Solars are going to be attacked by such effects very often?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say not a big deal so much as not an elementary concern, that neither Solar Integrity Charms nor Solar Psyche Charms were written with the assumption that they would be in opposition very often.<br /> <br /> I've also argued things like how these Psyche effects include their own defeat conditions, and that Integrity Charms focused on defending against or overcoming things like mind control place a greater priority on characterisation and the narrative of struggling against something like mind control, and even with mechanics I think there are some fairly generous effects, such as the one to greatly reduce the cost of the Integrity Excellency or the one to waive the cost of Charms to resist influence or control altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:49:38-07:00","id":908240,"title":"","content":"You may be right (I think I'd better give the Psyche charms and Integrity charms another look before weighing in), but one thing I will say is that reducing the cost of the Integrity excellency isn't massively significant. From what I've seen, people rarely apply their Integrity more than once or twice a scene, so it's saving 10 motes maximum. Not an insignificant benefit, because it gives you more motes for other things, but it doesn't really make you much better at resisting mental influence. Unless you're being targeted again and again (which I guess is going to generally require different social influence, since someone who fails to convince you of something can't just keep trying without something significant).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:58:39-07:00","id":908246,"title":"","content":"It might not make one better, but I think it strengthens the incentive for any player who has a mindset of conservation for future emergencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T04:04:47-07:00","id":908249,"title":"","content":"I also just noticed that it's only useable once per scene, so actually all it does is save you 3-5 motes in a social scene when using a full excellency (and you're right, it does likely make you more likely to use a full excellency).<br /> But I think Sanctaphrax is right about it not being that significant or reliable a defence, except against mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-06-2016, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T04:11:11-07:00","id":908251,"title":"","content":"Okay, looking at the Integrity charms, I think there are some that genuinely do help you resist powerful mind-altering effects made by things with fat dice pools (like Abyssals or Infernals or Sidereals... well, Sidereals have small dice pools, but, you know, Target Number 4). I mean, they're not like the old Elusive Dreams Defence, but that made social combat essentially a waste of time.<br /> <br /> Destiny-Manifesting Method downgrades (or makes you immune to, with the upgrade) &quot;a reality-shaping or fate-weaving attack that would permanently alter her mind&quot;. So wacky Sidereal psyche effects may well be covered by that.<br /> Transcendant Hero's Meditation should also help against most wacky psyche effects.<br /> <br /> Steel-Heart Stance means, once per story (with a reset condition that might well come up occasionally), when persuaded to do something significant, you can just ignore the successful social influence.<br /> <br /> Righteous Lion Defence perfectly defends against any social effect that would cause you to act against a Defining Principle. One of the PCs in my game has this for her intimacy of &quot;No Gods and no masters&quot; which has made her immune to the Zenith's common huge-dice-pool social influence attempts to get people to join his religion and worship the UCS.<br /> <br /> Unhesitating Dedication is, essentially, the cap-breaking boost Irked was arguing for (on behalf of Sanctaphrax? Lack of avatars makes it hard for me to keep track of who's saying what), so it does actually exist. It only works to stop people eroding your Defining Intimacies though, once per intimacy per story.<br /> <br /> Invincible Solar Aegis protects (as long as you properly uphold a Defining Intimacy) against &quot;Fiat-level alterations to her destiny. \u2022 Sorcerous curses such as the spell Corrupted Words. \u2022 Psychic assaults of any kind. \u2022 Magical attacks that would transform her body in some unwanted way.&quot; So that definitely protects against Psyche effects.<br /> <br /> To be honest, it looks to me like the wacky psyche effects of other splats is exactly what Solars <i>are</i> good at defending against. Regular, excellency-boosted social influence that doesn't go against their Defining Intimacies is what they have less defences against.<br /> <br /> Next I'll have a look at Psyche effects and whether they do indeed have ways to avoid them built-in, like Isator said.<br /> (You can probably tell I'm procastinating because I have real work for my job to do, that I don't want to do)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-06-2016, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T04:27:55-07:00","id":908255,"title":"","content":"Okay, I had a look at the Psyche effects, all of them explain how they can be defended against (generally by spending a bunch of wp, though in some cases it's only by using Transcendant Hero's Meditation... which is explicitly mentioned*) except for Essence-Laden Missive, and, as Sanctaphrax has said, Corrupted Words. Though I think that Corrupted Words is probably covered by some of the Integrity charms.<br /> Some of them you can only resist if they go against Defining intimacies, or people present evidence as to why you're wrong, and if you spend WP to ignore Hypnotic Tongue you forget that they hypnotised you.<br /> <br /> So, it seems to me like Solars don't really have much in the way of perfectly defending against stuff (except for outright magic curses), but do have various narrative ways to defend.<br /> So, when faced with a mind-control throwing huge-dice-pool Celestial, I think that the Integrity Solar will break free after some narrative drama. This may work well, or may not, it depends.<br /> <br /> It's certainly more interesting than the old &quot;use Integrity charms, ignore&quot;. But it does probably rely on the devs only writing social effect charms that are interesting in of themselves, and written in the way that influences the narrative in interesting ways rather than just &quot;you are my mind-slave now&quot; or &quot;you attack your friends instead now&quot;.<br /> <br /> *This, and the general way they're written, implies to me that the Solar Integrity and social influence/psyche charms were in fact, written under the assumption that they would be playing off against each other. Possibly as a model to ensure they still work later when other splat's charms go up against them, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-06-2016, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T07:26:16-07:00","id":908322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=908219#post908219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irked, are you saying Solars lack ways to reliably defend against mind-control and other very serious social attacks, whereas they do have ways to reliably defend against physical attacks (even if those cost a lot, but that's not the point)? That all they can do is boost their Resolve up to 10 (11 with a spec)?<br /> (I get the point about how making excellencies cheaper doesn't help with this, or other charms that increase your Resolve for cheap, like Elusive Dreams Defence or Temptating-Resisting Stance, since you can still only increase your Resolve by 5, but that's a seperate point)</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, my biggest dog in this fight is clarity, but yeah, that's the position I was defending. Or, well: specifically, that Solars have no ways of raising their Resolve higher, like they do for their Defense; they can spend Willpower like anybody else after the fact, if nothing else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't the favourability only slight though? I mean, if I have 21 dice and you have Resolve 11 (max pools) then I only have a very slight advantage over you, statistically.<br /> (I think, I haven't run the exact probability)<br /> I mean, you are right, but as far as I see it's a pretty small advantage. </div> </div> </div>It's only a little over 50%, yeah, but it's still more-likely-than-not that you lose when hit with a big mental effect.<br /> <br /> Unhesitating Dedication is a good catch! A lot of the other stuff is either very narrow (Righteous Lion - very potent, for exactly one Intimacy) or doesn't kick in until <i>after</i> you've stabbed your wife (Transcendent Hero's Meditation is built for going &quot;What have I done?&quot;), though. And, unfortunately, Unhesitating Dedication isn't going to be applicable in most of the really nasty stuff, because it only resists Instill actions - which very few of the big effects are. There's no general-purpose cap-booster that would apply against more general social magics.<br /> <br /> And so what do you do against, say, Memory-Reweaving Discipline, or Mind-Wiping Gaze?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T07:53:51-07:00","id":908337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=908322#post908322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only a little over 50%, yeah, but it's still more-likely-than-not that you lose when hit with a big mental effect.<br /> <br /> Unhesitating Dedication is a good catch! A lot of the other stuff is either very narrow (Righteous Lion - very potent, for exactly one Intimacy) or doesn't kick in until <i>after</i> you've stabbed your wife (Transcendent Hero's Meditation is built for going &quot;What have I done?&quot;), though. And, unfortunately, Unhesitating Dedication isn't going to be applicable in most of the really nasty stuff, because it only resists Instill actions - which very few of the big effects are. There's no general-purpose cap-booster that would apply against more general social magics.<br /> <br /> And so what do you do against, say, Memory-Reweaving Discipline, or Mind-Wiping Gaze?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, and I cannot emphasize this enough, Twisted Words Technique. I know keep throwing this out there, but that's because it's one stop shopping for beating every defense which gets brought up:<ul><li>It gets to target your strongest Intimacy, meaning that attack beats defense well over 50% of the time, since the attacker will get a big bonus from the strong Intimacy, and you may not have opposing Intimacies at all.</li> <li>Likewise, it'll never have to rely on Instill actions, Inspire actions, or eroding your (Righteous Lion-able) Intimacies. It does rely on Read Intentions, but you've got <i>forever</i> to study up on someone and guess that, hey, she really seems to hate slavery. Only then do you actually walk up to her and make her sell her family.</li> <li>Well, &quot;walk up to her&quot;. It's in Linguistics, so you don't actually have to be physically present at all when it goes off.</li> <li>You can't just spend Willpower to resist. You need someone else to dissuade you, and they're opposing your Resolve +2 (granted, you're probably not gonna Excellency this one). If you drop this awful thing on a group's social specialist (who is still helpless as anyone else to resist it), the less-erudite characters might legitimately have a hard time breaking them free. When they do, of course, it'll cost multiple Willpower to shake, so hopefully you've kept that on hand.</li> <li>For the same reason, I'm not sure whether you're allowed to fire off Transcendent Hero's Meditation, save as an alternative to the WP cost.</li> </ul><br /> In short, the only reliable defense is anti-Psyche tech (which is a pretty vague category, because the book never uses that Keyword in the descriptions of Charms which appear to be referencing it). And that's a little sad, when so many people were so keen on an edition without &quot;either have an explicit 'nope out of this' Charm or auto-lose&quot; as a concept.<br /> <br /> P.S.: Seven Omens Shot can have similar issues, in the sense of &quot;surprise negator or die,&quot; but at least that deigns to interact with the system at multiple points on the way.<br /> P.P.S.: Yes, if your opponent tags you with TWT targeting an Intimacy which you've got Righteous Lion Defense of, you agree to what they're saying, run off to betray everything that you hold dear, then are unable to do it (but don't understand why). Yes, that's awesome. But you only get one RLD, and I'd rather not turn the social interaction system into &quot;guess the RLD&quot; Battleship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:21:02-07:00","id":909098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904325-ex3-not-the-god-king-of-gaps-holes-in-the-solar-charm-set?p=908214#post908214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I mean, I do expect Lunars to be fairly lacking on the Craft front, but that's less because Solars have it and more because Lunars have had practically fuck all to help with artifacts for two editions running, and the fact that devs supposedly want to focus on the physical and barbarian rebel parts of their fluff doesn't seem a thing that would point to the streak being broken being the most likely of things :P.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah. Fair. I was not in any way implying we should expect Solar-level Craft suites out of anybody else. I do think it's fair to expect Lunars will have charms that enhance their Craft actions beyond the Excellency. The MoEP had two, I think? :P<br /> <br /> Also, I'm really happy I'm not the only one who noted the general lack of anti-influence charms in Integrity. I thought maybe I had missed some quirk of the system, or was misreading one of the charms. The suite is semi-useful for normal social influence, but cruddy if someone has a psyche charm, or just a well-endowed dice pool (ala cheap dice from Presence/Socialize).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}